{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784386579106,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_YdLF74sTfrYwWiD0a5FMxluE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md","offset":360,"limit":170},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n360: | Malformed or suspect tokens | Parse, schema-check, cap sizes, validate expected paths | Exclude record; never synthesize replacement values |\n361: | Mode authority drift | Keep hub/query capabilities generic; mode owns selection and taste | Reject retrieval result that changes routing or proof authority |\n362: | Context bloat | Five-card cap, mode-specific hydration, byte budgets | Truncate/refuse hydration, not silent full-document expansion |\n363: | Generic averaging | Exclusive dimension ownership and transformation ledger | Collapse to one source or derive from target |\n364: \n365: [SOURCE: iterations/iteration-007.md:30-42]\n366: \n367: ## 15. Implementation Sequence\n368: \n369: ### Phase A: Minimum viable utilization\n370: \n371: Estimated effort: 5-8 engineer-days.\n372: \n373: - deterministic retrieval-manifest schema and generator;\n374: - content/generation hashes and atomic `--write`/`--check`;\n375: - generic query cards and deterministic required-facet/exclusion filters;\n376: - bounded source-scan ranking/fallback;\n377: - generation-guarded hydration;\n378: - mode request adapters for interface, foundations, motion, audit, and md-generator;\n379: - `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema and fixtures;\n380: - CI selectors and change/invalidation tests.\n381: \n382: ### Phase B: Lexical acceleration and evaluation\n383: \n384: Estimated effort: +1-2 days for FTS, plus 2-4 planning days for benchmark curation.\n385: \n386: - disposable generation-bound FTS5 projection;\n387: - repeated-query and packaging benchmarks;\n388: - larger frozen human-labeled holdout;\n389: - paraphrases, required facets, explicit negatives, and hard-negative fixtures.\n390: \n391: ### Phase C: Conditional semantic trial\n392: \n393: Only proceed if Phase B demonstrates a material unresolved relevance gap.\n394: \n395: - build semantic projection against the same generation;\n396: - freeze prompts and labels before running rankers;\n397: - measure incremental lift after deterministic and lexical baseline;\n398: - promote only if lift justifies dependency, versioning, and rebuild cost.\n399: \n400: ## 16. References\n401: \n402: ### Iteration evidence\n403: \n404: - `iterations/iteration-001.md`: corpus inventory and mode-contract baseline.\n405: - `iterations/iteration-002.md`: substrate and repository-native precedent comparison.\n406: - `iterations/iteration-003.md`: first ranking and context-cost ablation.\n407: - `iterations/iteration-004.md`: mode consumption and one-versus-synthesis contract.\n408: - `iterations/iteration-005.md`: operational anti-slop gate and falsification.\n409: - `iterations/iteration-006.md`: build/query/refresh/validation lifecycle.\n410: - `iterations/iteration-007.md`: ranked strategies and corpus-wide risk analysis.\n411: - `iterations/iteration-008.md`: final human-auditable holdout and substrate closure.\n412: \n413: ### Primary repository sources\n414: \n415: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md`\n416: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-interface/SKILL.md`\n417: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-foundations/SKILL.md`\n418: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-motion/SKILL.md`\n419: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-audit/SKILL.md`\n420: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-md-generator/SKILL.md`\n421: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/shared/context_loading_contract.md`\n422: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_harness/README.md`\n423: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_harness/extract-refero.mjs`\n424: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_manifest.json`\n425: - `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md`\n426: - `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp_server/handlers/skill-graph/status.ts`\n427: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/lib/search/sqlite-fts.ts`\n428: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/lib/search/hybrid-search.ts`\n429: \n430: ### Corpus examples\n431: \n432: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/kobu/`\n433: - `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/19-86/`\n434: - the 27 manually inspected final-holdout `DESIGN.md` files listed in `iterations/iteration-008.md:20-24`.\n435: \n436: See `resource-map.md` for the reducer-generated evidence inventory. Some map rows include line-range suffixes as literal paths and are therefore marked `MISSING`; the underlying source files are cited correctly in the iteration narratives.\n437: \n438: ## 17. Convergence Report\n439: \n440: - Stop reason: `converged` via `all_questions_answered`.\n441: - Total iterations: 8 of 10 maximum.\n442: - Minimum iterations: 3, passed.\n443: - Questions answered: 5/5.\n444: - Remaining required questions: 0.\n445: - newInfoRatio trend: `1.00 -> 0.93 -> 0.83 -> 0.85 -> 0.93 -> 0.93 -> 0.85 -> 0.85`.\n446: - Average newInfoRatio: 0.896.\n447: - Last three ratios: `0.93 -> 0.85 -> 0.85`.\n448: - Convergence threshold: 0.05. Low-novelty convergence did not trigger; complete evidence-backed question coverage did.\n449: - Source diversity: 147 code/file references plus 18 other evidence entries in the reducer metrics.\n450: - Quality guards: minimum depth passed; 5/5 question coverage passed; source diversity passed; focus alignment passed; no single weak source dominated a required conclusion.\n451: - Graph convergence: no graph events were emitted, so graph blockers were absent and the inline legal-stop path remained authoritative.\n452: - Divergent pivots: none; convergence mode was `default`.\n453: - Non-blocking uncertainty: semantic lift and larger benchmark calibration remain future validation, explicitly excluded from baseline dependencies.\n454: \n455: [SOURCE: deep-research-dashboard.md:17-74] [SOURCE: deep-research-state.jsonl]\n\n(End of file - total 455 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"| Malformed or suspect tokens | Parse, schema-check, cap sizes, validate expected paths | Exclude record; never synthesize replacement values |\n| Mode authority drift | Keep hub/query capabilities generic; mode owns selection and taste | Reject retrieval result that changes routing or proof authority |\n| Context bloat | Five-card cap, mode-specific hydration, byte budgets | Truncate/refuse hydration, not silent full-document expansion |\n| Generic averaging | Exclusive dimension ownership and transformation ledger | Collapse to one source or derive from target |\n\n[SOURCE: iterations/iteration-007.md:30-42]\n\n## 15. Implementation Sequence\n\n### Phase A: Minimum viable utilization\n\nEstimated effort: 5-8 engineer-days.\n\n- deterministic retrieval-manifest schema and generator;\n- content/generation hashes and atomic `--write`/`--check`;\n- generic query cards and deterministic required-facet/exclusion filters;\n- bounded source-scan ranking/fallback;\n- generation-guarded hydration;\n- mode request adapters for interface, foundations, motion, audit, and md-generator;\n- `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema and fixtures;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md","text":"| Malformed or suspect tokens | Parse, schema-check, cap sizes, validate expected paths | Exclude record; never synthesize replacement values |\n| Mode authority drift | Keep hub/query capabilities generic; mode owns selection and taste | Reject retrieval result that changes routing or proof authority |\n| Context bloat | Five-card cap, mode-specific hydration, byte budgets | Truncate/refuse hydration, not silent full-document expansion |\n| Generic averaging | Exclusive dimension ownership and transformation ledger | Collapse to one source or derive from target |\n\n[SOURCE: iterations/iteration-007.md:30-42]\n\n## 15. Implementation Sequence\n\n### Phase A: Minimum viable utilization\n\nEstimated effort: 5-8 engineer-days.\n\n- deterministic retrieval-manifest schema and generator;\n- content/generation hashes and atomic `--write`/`--check`;\n- generic query cards and deterministic required-facet/exclusion filters;\n- bounded source-scan ranking/fallback;\n- generation-guarded hydration;\n- mode request adapters for interface, foundations, motion, audit, and md-generator;\n- `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema and fixtures;\n- CI selectors and change/invalidation tests.\n\n### Phase B: Lexical acceleration and evaluation\n\nEstimated effort: +1-2 days for FTS, plus 2-4 planning days for benchmark curation.\n\n- disposable generation-bound FTS5 projection;\n- repeated-query and packaging benchmarks;\n- larger frozen human-labeled holdout;\n- paraphrases, required facets, explicit negatives, and hard-negative fixtures.\n\n### Phase C: Conditional semantic trial\n\nOnly proceed if Phase B demonstrates a material unresolved relevance gap.\n\n- build semantic projection against the same generation;\n- freeze prompts and labels before running rankers;\n- measure incremental lift after deterministic and lexical baseline;\n- promote only if lift justifies dependency, versioning, and rebuild cost.\n\n## 16. References\n\n### Iteration evidence\n\n- `iterations/iteration-001.md`: corpus inventory and mode-contract baseline.\n- `iterations/iteration-002.md`: substrate and repository-native precedent comparison.\n- `iterations/iteration-003.md`: first ranking and context-cost ablation.\n- `iterations/iteration-004.md`: mode consumption and one-versus-synthesis contract.\n- `iterations/iteration-005.md`: operational anti-slop gate and falsification.\n- `iterations/iteration-006.md`: build/query/refresh/validation lifecycle.\n- `iterations/iteration-007.md`: ranked strategies and corpus-wide risk analysis.\n- `iterations/iteration-008.md`: final human-auditable holdout and substrate closure.\n\n### Primary repository sources\n\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-interface/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-foundations/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-motion/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-audit/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-md-generator/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/shared/context_loading_contract.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_harness/README.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_harness/extract-refero.mjs`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_manifest.json`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp_server/handlers/skill-graph/status.ts`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/lib/search/sqlite-fts.ts`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/lib/search/hybrid-search.ts`\n\n### Corpus examples\n\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/kobu/`\n- `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/19-86/`\n- the 27 manually inspected final-holdout `DESIGN.md` files listed in `iterations/iteration-008.md:20-24`.\n\nSee `resource-map.md` for the reducer-generated evidence inventory. Some map rows include line-range suffixes as literal paths and are therefore marked `MISSING`; the underlying source files are cited correctly in the iteration narratives.\n\n## 17. Convergence Report\n\n- Stop reason: `converged` via `all_questions_answered`.\n- Total iterations: 8 of 10 maximum.\n- Minimum iterations: 3, passed.\n- Questions answered: 5/5.\n- Remaining required questions: 0.\n- newInfoRatio trend: `1.00 -> 0.93 -> 0.83 -> 0.85 -> 0.93 -> 0.93 -> 0.85 -> 0.85`.\n- Average newInfoRatio: 0.896.\n- Last three ratios: `0.93 -> 0.85 -> 0.85`.\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05. Low-novelty convergence did not trigger; complete evidence-backed question coverage did.\n- Source diversity: 147 code/file references plus 18 other evidence entries in the reducer metrics.\n- Quality guards: minimum depth passed; 5/5 question coverage passed; source diversity passed; focus alignment passed; no single weak source dominated a required conclusion.\n- Graph convergence: no graph events were emitted, so graph blockers were absent and the inline legal-stop path remained authoritative.\n- Divergent pivots: none; convergence mode was `default`.\n- Non-blocking uncertainty: semantic lift and larger benchmark calibration remain future validation, explicitly excluded from baseline dependencies.\n\n[SOURCE: deep-research-dashboard.md:17-74] [SOURCE: deep-research-state.jsonl]","lineStart":360,"lineEnd":455,"totalLines":455,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md","time":{"start":1784386579100,"end":1784386579105}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_068c9289f1a503be016a5b9412c7788191a85cc0c340d90959"}},"id":"prt_f75ba6a1c001Z9eOmcoI56kJvp","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75ba2435001md3wuKwzbR2jvM"}}
