{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784386914255,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_TQ4lFpWC6vEu9XPlPTIrpR2v","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/review/lineages/sol-c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/review/lineages/sol-c/deep-review-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Review Strategy: sk-design Styles Utilization\n2: \n3: ## 1. TOPIC\n4: \n5: Review the phase-parent packet `.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization` for correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability across its ten child phases.\n6: \n7: ## 2. REVIEW CHARTER\n8: \n9: - Target: `.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization` (`spec-folder`)\n10: - Scope: the lean parent trio, canonical child planning/completion documents, and the three completed research syntheses\n11: - Resource Map Coverage: disabled because no parent `resource-map.md` existed at initialization\n12: - Execution: autonomous detached lineage `sol-c`\n13: \n14: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n15: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n16: - [x] D1 Correctness: state, phase order, status claims, invariants, and acceptance criteria\n17: - [x] D2 Security: rights, provenance, injection, copying, caching, and authority boundaries\n18: - [x] D3 Traceability: parent/child alignment, research-to-plan lineage, checklist evidence, and metadata parity\n19: - [ ] D4 Maintainability: document hygiene, naming, stable contracts, and safe follow-on execution\n20: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n21: \n22: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n23: \n24: - Do not implement any planned phase or modify target documents.\n25: - Do not review sibling fan-out lineage artifacts under `review/lineages/sol-a` or `review/lineages/sol-b`.\n26: - Do not audit the full 1,290-style corpus; inspect only cited exemplars or contracts when a finding requires them.\n27: \n28: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n29: \n30: - Stop at legal convergence after all four dimensions and both core traceability protocols have coverage plus one stabilization pass.\n31: - Stop unconditionally after 10 completed iterations.\n32: - Active P0 findings force FAIL but do not by themselves authorize target mutation.\n33: \n34: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n35: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n36: \n37: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n38: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n39: | D1 Correctness | CONDITIONAL | 1 | Phase ordering and planned statuses are sound; resume continuity is stale in the parent and research children 002-003. |\n40: | D2 Security | CONDITIONAL | 2 | Rights, cache, and authority controls align; the STUDY pre-prompt injection boundary is unspecified. |\n41: | D3 Traceability | CONDITIONAL | 3 | Core protocols executed: checklist evidence passes; spec/code is partial because F002 remains. Checklist denominators drift in six phases. |\n42: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n43: \n44: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n46: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n47: - **P1 (Major):** 3 active\n48: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n49: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +1 P1, +0 P2\n50: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n51: \n52: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n53: \n54: - Initialization resolved the phase-parent map directly from the parent `spec.md` and `graph-metadata.json`.\n55: - Recursive strict validation gave a clean structural baseline for every packet (iteration 1).\n56: \n57: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n58: \n59: - `memory_match_triggers` and `memory_context` both timed out; packet-local continuity is the source of truth.\n60: - The code graph is empty and excludes specs; structural review uses direct reads and exact searches.\n61: \n62: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not re