{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784386927255,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_yv5xTEWE8rW5xDZTYchT8Kgj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"verify-iteration\\.cjs|reduce-state\\.cjs|heartbeat|release-lock|acquire-lock","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review","include":"*.{md,yaml,yml,json,cjs,js}"},"output":"Found 49 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state_reducer_registry.md:\n  Line 31: | Findings registry | `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Regenerate from JSONL |\n\n  Line 32: | Dashboard | `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Regenerate from registry and latest events |\n\n  Line 33: | Strategy machine sections | `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Update from coverage and findings |\n\n  Line 100: Every finding emitted into the JSONL delta (`findingDetails[]`) MUST include a `content_hash` field computed per the two-tier match. `reduce-state.cjs` reads this field for synthesis dedup.\n\n  Line 106: - `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` is the reducer implementation.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep_review_strategy.md:\n  Line 208: - Files: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:\n  Line 26: - Added `scripts/reduce-state.cjs`: review-specific state reducer that parses the JSONL iteration log, the per-iteration `iteration-NNN.md` files, and the strategy file, then regenerates `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and the machine-owned strategy anchors. Idempotent: re-running with identical inputs produces byte-identical output.\n\n  Line 30: - `deep_review_config.json` now declares `reducerScriptPath` and `runtimeCapabilityResolver`, and both `spec_kit_deep-review_auto.yaml` and `spec_kit_deep-review_confirm.yaml` invoke the reducer via `node .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}` during `step_reduce_review_state` with an idempotency guarantee.\n\n  Line 74: | `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`                                                                | Created  | Review-specific reducer with finding lifecycle, dimension coverage, idempotent output      |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.3.0.0.md:\n  Line 71: | `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Modified | parseJsonlDetailed + fail-closed JSONL + fail-closed anchors + blockedStopHistory + graphConvergenceScore + persistentSameSeverity + severityChanged + dashboard sections |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.10.0.0.md:\n  Line 1: This release reconciles the legal-stop gate model across the `deep-review` documentation surfaces. The authoritative producer is `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`, which emits a 9-gate `gateResults` bundle. The documentation had drifted to describe 6 or 7 gates depending on the surface, omitting `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` (the two v2-rollout gates) and, in one table, `claimAdjudicationGate`. Every surface now enumerates the same 9 gates with the same `Gate`-suffix names, so a reader of any one document sees the model the runtime actually emits. This is a documentation-only release. The reducer (`scripts/reduce-state.cjs`) is gate-name-agnostic and was confirmed unchanged, and the YAML workflows were read-only as the source of truth.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/README.md:\n  Line 71: `reduce-state.cjs` relocated to the shared `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/` directory (promoted to a shared-runtime primitive); `deep-review`'s own callers now require/invoke it from that path.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.3.1.0.md:\n  Line 82: | `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Active Risks section widened to surface P1, claim-adjudication, and blocked-stop debt |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.3.2.0.md:\n  Line 14: The reducer ignored `synthesis_complete` events and derived dashboard status from stale config, so the dashboard never showed the actual stop reason or legal-stop outcome after a loop finished. `reduce-state.cjs` now parses the latest `synthesis_complete` JSONL record and derives `stopReason` and terminal legal-stop bundle from it.\n\n  Line 66: The agent definition (`deep-review.md`) iteration skeleton was internally contradictory - different heading names than the reducer parser expected. Collapsed to one main fenced template matching the sections `reduce-state.cjs` actually consumes.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md:\n  Line 60: - Let `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` be the SINGLE state writer\n\n  Line 374: 7. Use `generate-context.js` for continuity saves. **Owner**: the YAML workflow (`deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`) calls it at the save phase, not the reducer (`scripts/reduce-state.cjs`) directly — don't expect continuity-save side effects from the reducer alone.\n\n  Line 410: Scripts: `scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, `scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md:\n  Line 67: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder>\n\n  Line 138: | Reducer refuses to write derived state | `reduce-state.cjs` detected JSONL corruption | Repair the line or pass `--lenient` |\n\n  Line 209: | [`scripts/reduce-state.cjs`](./scripts/reduce-state.cjs) | The single state reducer that updates the findings registry, dashboard and strategy |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/review_depth_v2_rollout/reducer_search_debt.md:\n  Line 22: - Layer partition: reducer (`reduce-state.cjs`) + dashboard + report compiler.\n\n  Line 57: - Reducer: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` (registry return shape + dashboard verdict + active-risks rendering).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.9.0.0.md:\n  Line 9: The README, SKILL.md, and four reference files now align with the current sk-doc templates and pass HVR cleanly. No behavioral code shipped in this release. The reducer (`scripts/reduce-state.cjs`) was bug-scan only per the surgical-edit policy.\n\n  Line 75: | `reduce-state.cjs` syntax check (`node -c`) | PASS |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/review_depth_v2_rollout/stop_gate_candidate_coverage.md:\n  Line 58: - Reducer: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` (registry exposing `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep_review_config.json:\n  Line 58:   \"reducerScriptPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop_protocol.md:\n  Line 759: - `reduce-state.cjs` is the single state writer.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/tests/fixtures/blocked-stop-session/README.md:\n  Line 25: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs \\\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature_catalog/severity_system/convergence_signals.md:\n  Line 40: | `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Reducer | `computeConvergenceScore` and the registry stability inputs the signals draw from. |\n\n  Line 56: - Primary sources: `references/convergence/convergence.md`, `scripts/reduce-state.cjs`\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature_catalog/loop_lifecycle/resource_map_emission.md:\n  Line 40: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Reducer | Adds the `--emit-resource-map` path and honors `config.resource_map.emit`. |\n\n  Line 59: - Primary sources: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/resource-map/extract-from-evidence.cjs`, `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml`, `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_confirm.yaml`\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/tests/reduce-state-summary-fallback.test.cjs:\n  Line 12: const { reduceReviewState } = require('../../../runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs');\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/synthesis_save_and_guardrails/resource_map_emission.md:\n  Line 53: 2. `bash: rg -n 'resource_map|resource-map|emit-resource-map' .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_confirm.yaml .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`\n\n  Line 54: 3. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder> --emit-resource-map`\n\n  Line 55: 4. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder> --emit-resource-map` with `deep-review-config.json` edited to `\"resource_map\": { \"emit\": false }`\n\n  Line 91: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Reducer flag handling and write path |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/convergence_and_recovery/fail_closed_reducer.md:\n  Line 53: 1. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {corrupt_fixture}. Echo \"exit: $?\"`\n\n  Line 55: 3. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {anchor_fixture}. Echo \"exit: $?\"`\n\n  Line 56: 4. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {corrupt_fixture} --lenient. Echo \"exit: $?\"`\n\n  Line 58: 6. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {anchor_fixture} --create-missing-anchors. Echo \"exit: $?\"`\n\n  Line 71: Privilege `reduce-state.cjs` for exit semantics and `review-reducer-fail-closed.vitest.ts` for concrete expected behavior. If fixture preparation accidentally combines both failures in one directory, split into two fixture copies before judging the reducer.\n\n  Line 87: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Canonical reducer implementation, emits `corruptionWarnings`, exits non-zero on corruption, and enforces machine-owned anchor presence unless recovery flags are passed |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/convergence_and_recovery/blocked_stop_reducer_surfacing.md:\n  Line 29: - When: The operator runs `node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder>`.\n\n  Line 53: 1. `bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}`\n\n  Line 84: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Canonical reducer implementation, promotes `blocked_stop` into `blockedStopHistory`, renders `BLOCKED STOPS`, and rewrites `ANCHOR:next-focus` |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature_catalog/state_management/graph_convergence_event.md:\n  Line 39: | `scripts/reduce-state.cjs` | Reducer | `buildGraphConvergenceRollup` and `computeGraphConvergenceScore` roll events into registry history. |\n\n  Line 55: - Primary sources: `references/state/state_format.md`, `references/convergence/convergence.md`, `scripts/reduce-state.cjs`\n","metadata":{"matches":49,"truncated":false},"title":"verify-iteration\\.cjs|reduce-state\\.cjs|heartbeat|release-lock|acquire-lock","time":{"start":1784386927157,"end":1784386927240}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04cfb65b5f1fca05016a5b956f03948191ac8a5f0ac4b01acf"}},"id":"prt_f75bfb9e5001Tkf7UUWAb5tqUR","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75bf9366001gToAASFTDCHwiN"}}
