{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387007104,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ujQRjz85Nu7cHrThdG51frsG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md","offset":250,"limit":60},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n250: 1. Given a card whose generation hash matches the current manifest, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive the permitted artifacts/slices within the byte cap.\n251: 2. Given a stale card, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive `generation-mismatch` and no content.\n252: \n253: ### US-003: Proof-gated ready claim (Priority: P1)\n254: \n255: **As a** maintainer, **I want** any corpus-influenced ready claim blocked without a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card, **so that** un-provenanced or averaged output cannot ship.\n256: \n257: **Acceptance Criteria**:\n258: 1. Given corpus material influenced a decision, When a ready claim is made without a valid proof card, Then the gate blocks it.\n259: <!-- /ANCHOR:user-stories -->\n260: \n261: ---\n262: \n263: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n264: ## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n265: \n266: - Should the FTS accelerator ship with Phase A or wait for measured repeated-query load in Phase B? **Leaning: build the interface in Phase A, enable only when operational measurements justify it.**\n267: - Where should `_retrieval-manifest.json` live relative to `_engine/` for cleanest `styles/**` CI globbing? **RESOLVED: manifest at `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`, code under `styles/_engine/`.**\n268: - What is the exact facet vocabulary for `requiredFacets`/`exclusions`? **Deferred to implementation; seeded from research §5 examples (`serif-role`, `warm-surface`, `license-restricted`, `generation-mismatch`).**\n269: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n270: \n271: ---\n272: \n273: <!-- ANCHOR:related-docs -->\n274: ## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n275: \n276: - **Parent**: `../spec.md`\n277: - **Predecessor**: `../003-global-modes-utilization/`\n278: - **Successor**: `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/`\n279: - **Research basis**: `../001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md` (§4 substrate, §5 pipeline, §9 tooling, §15 Phase A)\n280: - **Source corpus**: `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/`\n281: - **Plan**: `plan.md` · **Tasks**: `tasks.md` · **Checklist**: `checklist.md` · **Decisions**: `decision-record.md`\n282: <!-- /ANCHOR:related-docs -->\n283: </content>\n284: </invoke>\n\n(End of file - total 284 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"1. Given a card whose generation hash matches the current manifest, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive the permitted artifacts/slices within the byte cap.\n2. Given a stale card, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive `generation-mismatch` and no content.\n\n### US-003: Proof-gated ready claim (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** maintainer, **I want** any corpus-influenced ready claim blocked without a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card, **so that** un-provenanced or averaged output cannot ship.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n1. Given corpus material influenced a decision, When a ready claim is made without a valid proof card, Then the gate blocks it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:user-stories -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Should the FTS accelerator ship with Phase A or wait for measured repeated-query load in Phase B? **Leaning: build the interface in Phase A, enable only when operational measurements justify it.**\n- Where should `_retrieval-manifest.json` live relative to `_engine/` for cleanest `styles/**` CI globbing? **RESOLVED: manifest at `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`, code under `styles/_engine/`.**\n- What is the exact facet vocabulary for `requiredFacets`/`exclusions`? **Deferred to implementation; seeded from research §5 examples (`serif-role`, `warm-surface`, `license-restricted`, `generation-mismatch`).**\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md","text":"1. Given a card whose generation hash matches the current manifest, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive the permitted artifacts/slices within the byte cap.\n2. Given a stale card, When I `hydrate`, Then I receive `generation-mismatch` and no content.\n\n### US-003: Proof-gated ready claim (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** maintainer, **I want** any corpus-influenced ready claim blocked without a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card, **so that** un-provenanced or averaged output cannot ship.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n1. Given corpus material influenced a decision, When a ready claim is made without a valid proof card, Then the gate blocks it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:user-stories -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Should the FTS accelerator ship with Phase A or wait for measured repeated-query load in Phase B? **Leaning: build the interface in Phase A, enable only when operational measurements justify it.**\n- Where should `_retrieval-manifest.json` live relative to `_engine/` for cleanest `styles/**` CI globbing? **RESOLVED: manifest at `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`, code under `styles/_engine/`.**\n- What is the exact facet vocabulary for `requiredFacets`/`exclusions`? **Deferred to implementation; seeded from research §5 examples (`serif-role`, `warm-surface`, `license-restricted`, `generation-mismatch`).**\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:related-docs -->\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Parent**: `../spec.md`\n- **Predecessor**: `../003-global-modes-utilization/`\n- **Successor**: `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/`\n- **Research basis**: `../001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md` (§4 substrate, §5 pipeline, §9 tooling, §15 Phase A)\n- **Source corpus**: `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/`\n- **Plan**: `plan.md` · **Tasks**: `tasks.md` · **Checklist**: `checklist.md` · **Decisions**: `decision-record.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:related-docs -->\n</content>\n</invoke>","lineStart":250,"lineEnd":284,"totalLines":284,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md","time":{"start":1784387007099,"end":1784387007103}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ed457b1cac8006e016a5b95be101481918f3a6e0a096c9d0c"}},"id":"prt_f75c0f1fd001H265wljjE725lA","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0c4a5001EE4XCbqVa4WRVq"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387007442,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_D5IYJEBKnyzqDgtlNaJjRBxw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md","offset":125,"limit":45},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n129: ## Architecture Decisions Summary\n130: \n131: | ADR | Decision | Status | Impact |\n132: |-----|----------|--------|--------|\n133: | ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | Proposed | Canonical, reviewable, hash-bound index |\n134: | ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Proposed | Composition/negation correctness; slop resistance |\n135: | ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Proposed | Fast ordering, no drift, uncommitted |\n136: | ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + source-scan fallback | Proposed | No stale-value leakage; resilient retrieval |\n137: | ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | Proposed | No un-provenanced/averaged corpus output ships |\n138: \n139: See `decision-record.md` for full ADR documentation. All five stay Proposed until the build validates.\n140: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: ## Follow-Up Items\n145: \n146: - [ ] Implement Phase 1-3 per `tasks.md` (T001-T028)\n147: - [ ] Decide FTS accelerator timing (Phase A vs Phase B)\n148: - [ ] Wire the engine into `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/`\n149: - [ ] Promote ADR-001..005 from Proposed to Accepted after the build validates\n150: </content>\n\n(End of file - total 150 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n## Architecture Decisions Summary\n\n| ADR | Decision | Status | Impact |\n|-----|----------|--------|--------|\n| ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | Proposed | Canonical, reviewable, hash-bound index |\n| ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Proposed | Composition/negation correctness; slop resistance |\n| ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Proposed | Fast ordering, no drift, uncommitted |\n| ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + source-scan fallback | Proposed | No stale-value leakage; resilient retrieval |\n| ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | Proposed | No un-provenanced/averaged corpus output ships |\n\nSee `decision-record.md` for full ADR documentation. All five stay Proposed until the build validates.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n\n---\n\n## Follow-Up Items","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md","text":"\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n## Architecture Decisions Summary\n\n| ADR | Decision | Status | Impact |\n|-----|----------|--------|--------|\n| ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | Proposed | Canonical, reviewable, hash-bound index |\n| ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Proposed | Composition/negation correctness; slop resistance |\n| ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Proposed | Fast ordering, no drift, uncommitted |\n| ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + source-scan fallback | Proposed | No stale-value leakage; resilient retrieval |\n| ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | Proposed | No un-provenanced/averaged corpus output ships |\n\nSee `decision-record.md` for full ADR documentation. All five stay Proposed until the build validates.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture-summary -->\n\n---\n\n## Follow-Up Items\n\n- [ ] Implement Phase 1-3 per `tasks.md` (T001-T028)\n- [ ] Decide FTS accelerator timing (Phase A vs Phase B)\n- [ ] Wire the engine into `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/`\n- [ ] Promote ADR-001..005 from Proposed to Accepted after the build validates\n</content>","lineStart":125,"lineEnd":150,"totalLines":150,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md","time":{"start":1784387007430,"end":1784387007441}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ed457b1cac8006e016a5b95be102c81919339bc396e330cad"}},"id":"prt_f75c0f29a0014WT1sj7jVN41vw","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0c4a5001EE4XCbqVa4WRVq"}}
