{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387027491,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_82juDgfrNJFTLVgbWavbBqlG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md","offset":325,"limit":45},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n325: | M2 | Eligibility | Facet/exclusion/provenance gates first | Day 3 |\n326: | M3 | Retrieval | Ranked cards + degraded fallback | Day 5 |\n327: | M4 | Hydration | Generation-guarded, mode-scoped | Day 6 |\n328: | M5 | Gated + CI | Proof gate + all invalidation fixtures | Day 7-8 |\n329: <!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n330: \n331: ---\n332: \n333: ## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n334: \n335: See `decision-record.md` for full ADRs:\n336: \n337: | ADR | Decision | Rationale |\n338: |-----|----------|-----------|\n339: | ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | ~503 KB, ~1 ms scans; canonical, cheap, reviewable |\n340: | ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Required-facets/negation need determinism (P@5 0.60 vs BM25 0.33) |\n341: | ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Cheap (~180 ms build), never authoritative, no drift risk |\n342: | ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + bounded source-scan fallback | Refuse stale values; degrade, never fail hard |\n343: | ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | No un-provenanced or averaged corpus-influenced claim ships |\n344: \n345: ---\n346: \n347: ## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n348: \n349: - **Specification**: `spec.md`\n350: - **Tasks**: `tasks.md`\n351: - **Checklist**: `checklist.md`\n352: - **Decisions**: `decision-record.md`\n353: - **Parent**: `../spec.md`\n354: </content>\n\n(End of file - total 354 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"| M2 | Eligibility | Facet/exclusion/provenance gates first | Day 3 |\n| M3 | Retrieval | Ranked cards + degraded fallback | Day 5 |\n| M4 | Hydration | Generation-guarded, mode-scoped | Day 6 |\n| M5 | Gated + CI | Proof gate + all invalidation fixtures | Day 7-8 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\nSee `decision-record.md` for full ADRs:\n\n| ADR | Decision | Rationale |\n|-----|----------|-----------|\n| ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | ~503 KB, ~1 ms scans; canonical, cheap, reviewable |\n| ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Required-facets/negation need determinism (P@5 0.60 vs BM25 0.33) |\n| ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Cheap (~180 ms build), never authoritative, no drift risk |\n| ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + bounded source-scan fallback | Refuse stale values; degrade, never fail hard |\n| ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | No un-provenanced or averaged corpus-influenced claim ships |\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md","text":"| M2 | Eligibility | Facet/exclusion/provenance gates first | Day 3 |\n| M3 | Retrieval | Ranked cards + degraded fallback | Day 5 |\n| M4 | Hydration | Generation-guarded, mode-scoped | Day 6 |\n| M5 | Gated + CI | Proof gate + all invalidation fixtures | Day 7-8 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\nSee `decision-record.md` for full ADRs:\n\n| ADR | Decision | Rationale |\n|-----|----------|-----------|\n| ADR-001 | Committed checked manifest is the only retrieval artifact | ~503 KB, ~1 ms scans; canonical, cheap, reviewable |\n| ADR-002 | Deterministic eligibility decides; scores only order | Required-facets/negation need determinism (P@5 0.60 vs BM25 0.33) |\n| ADR-003 | Disposable same-generation FTS5/BM25 accelerator | Cheap (~180 ms build), never authoritative, no drift risk |\n| ADR-004 | Generation-guarded hydration + bounded source-scan fallback | Refuse stale values; degrade, never fail hard |\n| ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | No un-provenanced or averaged corpus-influenced claim ships |\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Specification**: `spec.md`\n- **Tasks**: `tasks.md`\n- **Checklist**: `checklist.md`\n- **Decisions**: `decision-record.md`\n- **Parent**: `../spec.md`\n</content>","lineStart":325,"lineEnd":354,"totalLines":354,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md","time":{"start":1784387027486,"end":1784387027490}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_049a62f6a112f532016a5b95d31320819199a59d646c911c91"}},"id":"prt_f75c1416f001LbKTcwzW5c52Yt","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0fdba001mERY0fJtEb0OCQ"}}
