{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387027870,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OGz5xEGGWvwdESud5mVFmob6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md","offset":180,"limit":45},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n180: <!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: <!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n185: ## L3+: DOCUMENTATION VERIFICATION\n186: \n187: - [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n188: - [ ] CHK-141 [P1] Manifest schema + candidate-card shape documented for downstream phases\n189: - [ ] CHK-142 [P2] Mode request/hydration adapter contract documented\n190: - [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer to `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/` documented\n191: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: <!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n196: ## L3+: SIGN-OFF\n197: \n198: | Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n199: |----------|------|--------|------|\n200: | pending | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n201: | pending | Design Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n202: | pending | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n203: <!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: <!--\n208: Level 3 checklist — Planned scaffold.\n209: All items UNCHECKED until the engine is built.\n210: P0 must complete, P1 need approval to defer.\n211: -->\n212: </content>\n\n(End of file - total 212 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: DOCUMENTATION VERIFICATION\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] Manifest schema + candidate-card shape documented for downstream phases\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] Mode request/hydration adapter contract documented\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer to `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/` documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: SIGN-OFF\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md","text":"<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: DOCUMENTATION VERIFICATION\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] Manifest schema + candidate-card shape documented for downstream phases\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] Mode request/hydration adapter contract documented\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer to `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/` documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: SIGN-OFF\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| pending | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| pending | Design Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| pending | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n\n<!--\nLevel 3 checklist — Planned scaffold.\nAll items UNCHECKED until the engine is built.\nP0 must complete, P1 need approval to defer.\n-->\n</content>","lineStart":180,"lineEnd":212,"totalLines":212,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md","time":{"start":1784387027866,"end":1784387027869}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_049a62f6a112f532016a5b95d3134481918ddf4ed953098fb5"}},"id":"prt_f75c1433d001kq6wxLzXaFC2Nh","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0fdba001mERY0fJtEb0OCQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387028022,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Fa6vvvAIlICJYxR8Csl8RrKA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md","offset":300,"limit":45},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n300: ### Alternatives Considered\n301: \n302: | Option | Pros | Cons | Score |\n303: |--------|------|------|-------|\n304: | **CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 blocking gate** | Blocks slop, averaging, and rights leakage | Requires a proof card per corpus-influenced claim | 9/10 |\n305: | Advisory-only proof | Lower friction | Un-provenanced output can ship | 3/10 |\n306: | No gate | Fast | Averaging + copy-exposure risk | 1/10 |\n307: \n308: **Why this one**: a blocking gate is the only reliable defense against averaged, un-provenanced, or rights-unknown corpus output. [SOURCE: research.md §7, §8, §14]\n309: \n310: ### Consequences\n311: \n312: **What improves**: no un-provenanced/averaged corpus-influenced claim ships; auditable decisions.\n313: **What it costs**: per-claim proof overhead . Mitigation: one coherent anchor by default keeps the proof compact.\n314: \n315: **Risks**:\n316: \n317: | Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n318: |------|--------|------------|\n319: | Proof card faked/empty | H | Schema validator + fixtures (T021/T027) |\n320: | Gate bypassed | H | Ready claim blocked without valid card (T022) |\n321: \n322: ### Implementation\n323: \n324: **What changes**: `styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs` (NEW).\n325: **How to roll back**: N/A — removing the gate reintroduces slop risk.\n326: \n327: ---\n328: \n329: <!--\n330: Level 3 Decision Record — Planned scaffold.\n331: Five ADRs, all Proposed until the engine is built and validated.\n332: -->\n333: </content>\n\n(End of file - total 333 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"### Alternatives Considered\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Score |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| **CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 blocking gate** | Blocks slop, averaging, and rights leakage | Requires a proof card per corpus-influenced claim | 9/10 |\n| Advisory-only proof | Lower friction | Un-provenanced output can ship | 3/10 |\n| No gate | Fast | Averaging + copy-exposure risk | 1/10 |\n\n**Why this one**: a blocking gate is the only reliable defense against averaged, un-provenanced, or rights-unknown corpus output. [SOURCE: research.md §7, §8, §14]\n\n### Consequences\n\n**What improves**: no un-provenanced/averaged corpus-influenced claim ships; auditable decisions.\n**What it costs**: per-claim proof overhead . Mitigation: one coherent anchor by default keeps the proof compact.\n\n**Risks**:\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|--------|------------|\n| Proof card faked/empty | H | Schema validator + fixtures (T021/T027) |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md","text":"### Alternatives Considered\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Score |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| **CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 blocking gate** | Blocks slop, averaging, and rights leakage | Requires a proof card per corpus-influenced claim | 9/10 |\n| Advisory-only proof | Lower friction | Un-provenanced output can ship | 3/10 |\n| No gate | Fast | Averaging + copy-exposure risk | 1/10 |\n\n**Why this one**: a blocking gate is the only reliable defense against averaged, un-provenanced, or rights-unknown corpus output. [SOURCE: research.md §7, §8, §14]\n\n### Consequences\n\n**What improves**: no un-provenanced/averaged corpus-influenced claim ships; auditable decisions.\n**What it costs**: per-claim proof overhead . Mitigation: one coherent anchor by default keeps the proof compact.\n\n**Risks**:\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|--------|------------|\n| Proof card faked/empty | H | Schema validator + fixtures (T021/T027) |\n| Gate bypassed | H | Ready claim blocked without valid card (T022) |\n\n### Implementation\n\n**What changes**: `styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs` (NEW).\n**How to roll back**: N/A — removing the gate reintroduces slop risk.\n\n---\n\n<!--\nLevel 3 Decision Record — Planned scaffold.\nFive ADRs, all Proposed until the engine is built and validated.\n-->\n</content>","lineStart":300,"lineEnd":333,"totalLines":333,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md","time":{"start":1784387028012,"end":1784387028020}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_049a62f6a112f532016a5b95d31350819182503fb87cf5bd87"}},"id":"prt_f75c143c5001r2hfP1R5bZ8Eqw","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0fdba001mERY0fJtEb0OCQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387028068,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_RL7dnB96Mq9fxuE7KyU5grKG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"T0(?:0[1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-9])","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate","include":"tasks.md"},"output":"Found 32 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/tasks.md:\n  Line 16:     next_safe_action: \"Start T001 — draft the manifest schema header and per-style fields\"\n\n  Line 63: - Eligibility (T007-T009) MUST land before ranking (T011+) — never invert the order.\n\n  Line 79: - [ ] T001 Draft manifest header (`schemaVersion`, `generationHash`, `crawlManifestHash`, `recordCount`, sorted `styles[]`) (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [2h]\n\n  Line 80: - [ ] T002 Define per-style fields (id/slug/status/title/thesis, token axes+counts, capabilities, sections, provenance/rights, artifact records, `contentHash`) (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T001}\n\n  Line 81: - [ ] T003 Implement refresh algorithm: enumerate/sort inputs, hash bytes, reparse only changed, remove deleted (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T002}\n\n  Line 82: - [ ] T004 Compute generation hash over schema + crawl-manifest hash + sorted content hashes (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T003}\n\n  Line 83: - [ ] T005 Implement atomic `build --write` (temp file + rename) and `corpus-changing` abort on fingerprint drift (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T004}\n\n  Line 84: - [ ] T006 Implement `build --check` (in-memory regen, byte-compare, report added/changed/removed ids, never write) (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T005}\n\n  Line 95: - [ ] T007 Implement required-facet filter (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T006}\n\n  Line 96: - [ ] T008 Implement exclusion filter (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T007}\n\n  Line 97: - [ ] T009 Implement provenance/rights gate (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T008}\n\n  Line 98: - [ ] T010 Guarantee eligibility runs before ranking; add ordering invariant test (`styles/_engine/__tests__/eligibility-first.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T009}\n\n  Line 101: - [ ] T011 Build disposable same-generation SQLite FTS5/BM25 projection from the current manifest (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T010}\n\n  Line 102: - [ ] T012 Ensure the FTS projection is never committed and is discarded after use (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [1h] {deps: T011}\n\n  Line 103: - [ ] T013 [P] Implement bounded `DESIGN.md` source-scan fallback returning `degraded:true` (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T010}\n\n  Line 104: - [ ] T014 Implement deterministic tie-breaking and stable card ordering (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T011, T013}\n\n  Line 107: - [ ] T015 Implement compact candidate cards (≤5, byte-capped, score breakdown, provenance, est. hydration bytes) (`styles/_engine/cards.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T014}\n\n  Line 108: - [ ] T016 Wire `query` command to eligibility → rank → cards (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T015}\n\n  Line 109: - [ ] T017 Implement generation-guarded hydration: require card generation hash, re-hash selected artifacts (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T016}\n\n  Line 110: - [ ] T018 Refuse `generation-mismatch`; return `unavailable` on stale selected artifacts (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T017}\n\n  Line 111: - [ ] T019 Apply mode-scoped includes and byte caps to hydration output (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T017}\n\n  Line 112: - [ ] T020 Wire `hydrate` command to the guard + mode scoping (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T018, T019}\n\n  Line 115: - [ ] T021 Implement `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema (authority, selection rationale, coherent fingerprint, transformation delta, provenance/anti-copy, application proof) (`styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T020}\n\n  Line 116: - [ ] T022 Block corpus-influenced ready claims without a valid proof card (`styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T021}\n\n  Line 126: - [ ] T023 Fixture: byte-stable `build --check` on unchanged corpus (`styles/_engine/__tests__/check-stable.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T006}\n\n  Line 127: - [ ] T024 Fixture: add/change/delete invalidation + pre/post mutation abort (`styles/_engine/__tests__/invalidation.test.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T023}\n\n  Line 128: - [ ] T025 [P] Fixture: stale/absent FTS → source-scan `degraded:true` (`styles/_engine/__tests__/fallback.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T013}\n\n  Line 129: - [ ] T026 [P] Fixture: generation-mismatch hydration refusal (`styles/_engine/__tests__/hydrate-guard.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T018}\n\n  Line 130: - [ ] T027 [P] Fixture: deterministic card ordering + valid/invalid proof cards (`styles/_engine/__tests__/proof.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T014, T022}\n\n  Line 131: - [ ] T028 Add CI selectors on `styles/**`, the engine, and mode contracts (`.opencode/skills/sk-design/**` CI config) [2h] {deps: T024, T025, T026, T027}\n\n  Line 139: - [ ] T029 Confirm each engine module maps to exactly one ADR authority (manifest→ADR-001, eligibility→ADR-002, rank-fts→ADR-003, hydrate→ADR-004, corpus-use-proof→ADR-005) (`decision-record.md`) [1h] {deps: T022}\n\n  Line 140: - [ ] T030 Promote ADR-001..005 from Proposed to Accepted after the build validates (`decision-record.md`) [1h] {deps: T028}\n","metadata":{"matches":32,"truncated":false},"title":"T0(?:0[1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-9])","time":{"start":1784387028055,"end":1784387028067}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_049a62f6a112f532016a5b95d313588191b709132f9811d1fe"}},"id":"prt_f75c1444d001Ut2Rw0STjOS4rb","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0fdba001mERY0fJtEb0OCQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387028176,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_YIeHIuLJirUEz73GRZpt47g5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"(?:styles/_engine|_retrieval-manifest|CORPUS_USE_PROOF|retrieval substrate)","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Decision Record: styles-library retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 3: description: \"Architecture decisions for the Phase A retrieval engine over the sk-design styles library: committed checked manifest, deterministic-eligibility authority, disposable FTS accelerator, generation-guarded hydration, and the CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 gate. Proposed; scaffold not yet built.\"\n\n  Line 5:   - \"retrieval substrate decisions\"\n\n  Line 30: # Decision Record: styles-library retrieval substrate\n\n  Line 69: **We chose**: generate one committed retrieval manifest, `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`, as the single canonical retrieval artifact; everything else (FTS, future vectors) stays disposable.\n\n  Line 131: - `styles/_engine/manifest.mjs` (NEW): schema, refresh, hashing.\n\n  Line 132: - `styles/_engine/style-library.mjs` (NEW): `build --write`/`--check`.\n\n  Line 133: - `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json` (NEW): the committed artifact.\n\n  Line 135: **How to roll back**: delete `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json` and `styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`; the corpus is untouched and no mode consumes the manifest until `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/`.\n\n  Line 183: **What changes**: `styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs` (NEW), `styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs` (NEW).\n\n  Line 230: **What changes**: `styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs` (NEW).\n\n  Line 277: **What changes**: `styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs` (NEW), `styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs` (NEW).\n\n  Line 282: ## ADR-005: CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 as a Blocking Ready-Gate\n\n  Line 294: Corpus material can silently distort output: an anchor chosen only because it ranked first, averaged token values, or reuse of source-specific assets under unknown rights. The research defines `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` as a blocking evidence card whenever corpus material influences a design decision.\n\n  Line 298: **We chose**: require a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card before any corpus-influenced ready claim. **Anti-slop / authority rule** (restated in spec §2/§4): deterministic eligibility decides; scores only explain ordering; one coherent anchor by default; never average token values. The card asserts authority, selection rationale, coherent fingerprint, transformation delta, provenance/anti-copy, and application proof.\n\n  Line 304: | **CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 blocking gate** | Blocks slop, averaging, and rights leakage | Requires a proof card per corpus-influenced claim | 9/10 |\n\n  Line 324: **What changes**: `styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs` (NEW).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Feature Specification: styles-library retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 3: description: \"Build the committed, resumable, generation-bound retrieval engine over the 1,290-bundle sk-design styles library that phase 001 Phase A recommended: a checked retrieval manifest, deterministic eligibility, a disposable FTS5/BM25 accelerator, compact candidate cards, generation-guarded hydration, and a CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 gate. Foundation phase; everything else in packet 011 depends on it.\"\n\n  Line 5:   - \"styles retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 33: # Feature Specification: styles-library retrieval substrate\n\n  Line 43: This phase builds the shared retrieval substrate for the 1,290-bundle styles library at `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/` — the foundation the completed research (`../001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md`, §4, §5, §9, §15 Phase A) ranked first (leverage 5, cost 5-8 days, reversibility 5). It delivers a committed, checked retrieval manifest; deterministic eligibility applied before any ranking; a disposable, same-generation SQLite FTS5/BM25 projection; compact candidate cards; generation-guarded hydration; and a blocking `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` gate. Every downstream phase in packet 011 (md-generator schema contract, global-mode consumption, guardrails) consumes this substrate, so it is authored and built first.\n\n  Line 45: **Key Decisions**: canonical committed manifest as the only retrieval artifact (ADR-001), deterministic eligibility decides / scores only explain ordering (ADR-002), disposable same-generation FTS accelerator (ADR-003), generation-guarded hydration with a live source-scan fallback (ADR-004), `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` as a blocking ready-gate (ADR-005).\n\n  Line 77: Build the Phase A retrieval substrate the research specified: a deterministic, resumable, generation-bound engine that (1) generates and checks a committed retrieval manifest, (2) filters by deterministic eligibility before ranking, (3) ranks eligible candidates with a disposable same-generation lexical projection, (4) returns compact candidate cards for mode-owned selection, (5) hydrates only the chosen style's permitted artifacts under a generation guard, and (6) blocks any corpus-influenced ready claim behind `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1`. This is the foundation every other phase in packet 011 builds on.\n\n  Line 90: - A `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` gate required before any corpus-influenced ready claim.\n\n  Line 104: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/style-library.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | CLI entrypoint: `build --write`, `build --check`, `query`, `hydrate` |\n\n  Line 105: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/manifest.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Manifest schema, refresh algorithm, content/generation hashing |\n\n  Line 106: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Required-facet, exclusion, and provenance/rights gates (pre-ranking) |\n\n  Line 107: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Disposable same-generation SQLite FTS5/BM25 projection + source-scan fallback |\n\n  Line 108: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/cards.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Compact candidate-card assembly and byte-capping |\n\n  Line 109: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Generation-guarded hydration of permitted artifacts/slices |\n\n  Line 110: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs` | Create (NEW/proposed) | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema + validator |\n\n  Line 111: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_retrieval-manifest.json` | Create (NEW/proposed) | The only committed retrieval artifact (byte-stable generated output) |\n\n  Line 112: | `.opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/_engine/__tests__/**` | Create (NEW/proposed) | Change/invalidation, fallback, generation-mismatch, and proof-card fixtures |\n\n  Line 124: | REQ-001 | Committed checked manifest | `build --write` produces byte-stable `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json` with `schemaVersion`, `generationHash`, `crawlManifestHash`, `recordCount`, and sorted `styles[]`; `build --check` regenerates in memory, byte-compares, reports added/changed/removed ids, and never writes. |\n\n  Line 127: | REQ-004 | CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 gate | No corpus-influenced ready claim is emitted without a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card (authority, selection rationale, coherent fingerprint, transformation delta, provenance/anti-copy, application proof). |\n\n  Line 147: - **SC-004**: A corpus-influenced ready claim is blocked unless a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card is present.\n\n  Line 160: | Risk | Averaged / slop output | Med | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocks; never average token values; one coherent anchor by default |\n\n  Line 228: | R-004 | Averaged / incoherent slop output | M | M | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking gate; one-anchor default |\n\n  Line 255: **As a** maintainer, **I want** any corpus-influenced ready claim blocked without a valid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` card, **so that** un-provenanced or averaged output cannot ship.\n\n  Line 267: - Where should `_retrieval-manifest.json` live relative to `_engine/` for cleanest `styles/**` CI globbing? **RESOLVED: manifest at `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`, code under `styles/_engine/`.**\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Implementation Plan: styles-library retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 3: description: \"Phased plan to build the Phase A retrieval engine over the 1,290-bundle sk-design styles library: checked manifest generator, deterministic eligibility, disposable FTS5/BM25 accelerator, candidate cards, generation-guarded hydration, CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 gate, and CI invalidation fixtures. Scaffold only; not yet built.\"\n\n  Line 5:   - \"retrieval substrate plan\"\n\n  Line 30: # Implementation Plan: styles-library retrieval substrate\n\n  Line 46: | **Committed artifact** | `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json` (byte-stable) only |\n\n  Line 47: | **Testing** | Vitest/node test fixtures under `styles/_engine/__tests__/` |\n\n  Line 50: Implement the Phase A substrate from `../001-research-utilization/research/lineages/sol/research.md` §15. A single local executable (`style-library.mjs`) exposes `build --write`, `build --check`, `query`, and `hydrate`. The manifest is the only committed retrieval artifact; the FTS5/BM25 projection is built on demand and discarded. Deterministic eligibility runs before ranking; hydration is generation-guarded; `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` gates any corpus-influenced ready claim. No watcher or daemon — the corpus rebuild is sub-second.\n\n  Line 68: - [ ] `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocks an unproven ready claim\n\n  Line 78: Layered hybrid retrieval (research §4): canonical committed manifest → deterministic eligibility → disposable same-generation lexical ranking → bounded candidate cards → mode-owned selection → generation-guarded hydration → `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1`.\n\n  Line 81: - **style-library.mjs** (`styles/_engine/`): CLI entrypoint dispatching `build`/`query`/`hydrate`.\n\n  Line 87: - **corpus-use-proof.mjs**: `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema + validator.\n\n  Line 91: build --write ──> _retrieval-manifest.json (committed, generation-hashed)\n\n  Line 101:               CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 ──> ready claim (blocked if invalid)\n\n  Line 107: │                 styles/_engine/style-library.mjs               │\n\n  Line 121: │                                    (CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1)        │\n\n  Line 154: - [ ] `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema + validator\n\n  Line 171: | Proof | valid/invalid `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` cards | fixtures | Both polarities |\n\n  Line 194: - **Procedure**: delete `styles/_engine/` and `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`; the corpus is untouched, and no mode yet depends on the engine at runtime until `../005-md-generator-schema-contract/` wires it in.\n\n  Line 241: 1. Remove `styles/_engine/` modules and `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`.\n\n  Line 290: | manifest.mjs | corpus | `_retrieval-manifest.json`, generation hash | eligibility, rank, hydrate |\n\n  Line 343: | ADR-005 | `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocking ready-gate | No un-provenanced or averaged corpus-influenced claim ships |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Verification Checklist: styles-library retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 5:   - \"retrieval substrate checklist\"\n\n  Line 16:     next_safe_action: \"Verify items as each engine module lands under styles/_engine/\"\n\n  Line 30: # Verification Checklist: styles-library retrieval substrate\n\n  Line 101: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` blocks unproven corpus-influenced ready claims (REQ-004, SC-004)\n\n  Line 120: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Engine under `styles/_engine/`; manifest at `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/tasks.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Tasks: styles-library retrieval substrate\"\n\n  Line 3: description: \"Run queue for building the Phase A retrieval engine: manifest generator, deterministic eligibility, disposable FTS accelerator, candidate cards, generation-guarded hydration, CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1 gate, and CI invalidation fixtures. Every task pending; nothing built.\"\n\n  Line 5:   - \"retrieval substrate tasks\"\n\n  Line 30: # Tasks: styles-library retrieval substrate\n\n  Line 57: - [ ] Confirm the target file is under `styles/_engine/` or is `styles/_retrieval-manifest.json`; refuse writes elsewhere.\n\n  Line 79: - [ ] T001 Draft manifest header (`schemaVersion`, `generationHash`, `crawlManifestHash`, `recordCount`, sorted `styles[]`) (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [2h]\n\n  Line 80: - [ ] T002 Define per-style fields (id/slug/status/title/thesis, token axes+counts, capabilities, sections, provenance/rights, artifact records, `contentHash`) (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T001}\n\n  Line 81: - [ ] T003 Implement refresh algorithm: enumerate/sort inputs, hash bytes, reparse only changed, remove deleted (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T002}\n\n  Line 82: - [ ] T004 Compute generation hash over schema + crawl-manifest hash + sorted content hashes (`styles/_engine/manifest.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T003}\n\n  Line 83: - [ ] T005 Implement atomic `build --write` (temp file + rename) and `corpus-changing` abort on fingerprint drift (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T004}\n\n  Line 84: - [ ] T006 Implement `build --check` (in-memory regen, byte-compare, report added/changed/removed ids, never write) (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T005}\n\n  Line 95: - [ ] T007 Implement required-facet filter (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T006}\n\n  Line 96: - [ ] T008 Implement exclusion filter (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T007}\n\n  Line 97: - [ ] T009 Implement provenance/rights gate (`styles/_engine/eligibility.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T008}\n\n  Line 98: - [ ] T010 Guarantee eligibility runs before ranking; add ordering invariant test (`styles/_engine/__tests__/eligibility-first.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T009}\n\n  Line 101: - [ ] T011 Build disposable same-generation SQLite FTS5/BM25 projection from the current manifest (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T010}\n\n  Line 102: - [ ] T012 Ensure the FTS projection is never committed and is discarded after use (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [1h] {deps: T011}\n\n  Line 103: - [ ] T013 [P] Implement bounded `DESIGN.md` source-scan fallback returning `degraded:true` (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T010}\n\n  Line 104: - [ ] T014 Implement deterministic tie-breaking and stable card ordering (`styles/_engine/rank-fts.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T011, T013}\n\n  Line 107: - [ ] T015 Implement compact candidate cards (≤5, byte-capped, score breakdown, provenance, est. hydration bytes) (`styles/_engine/cards.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T014}\n\n  Line 108: - [ ] T016 Wire `query` command to eligibility → rank → cards (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T015}\n\n  Line 109: - [ ] T017 Implement generation-guarded hydration: require card generation hash, re-hash selected artifacts (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T016}\n\n  Line 110: - [ ] T018 Refuse `generation-mismatch`; return `unavailable` on stale selected artifacts (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T017}\n\n  Line 111: - [ ] T019 Apply mode-scoped includes and byte caps to hydration output (`styles/_engine/hydrate.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T017}\n\n  Line 112: - [ ] T020 Wire `hydrate` command to the guard + mode scoping (`styles/_engine/style-library.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T018, T019}\n\n  Line 115: - [ ] T021 Implement `CORPUS_USE_PROOF v1` schema (authority, selection rationale, coherent fingerprint, transformation delta, provenance/anti-copy, application proof) (`styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs`) [4h] {deps: T020}\n\n  Line 116: - [ ] T022 Block corpus-influenced ready claims without a valid proof card (`styles/_engine/corpus-use-proof.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T021}\n\n  Line 126: - [ ] T023 Fixture: byte-stable `build --check` on unchanged corpus (`styles/_engine/__tests__/check-stable.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T006}\n\n  Line 127: - [ ] T024 Fixture: add/change/delete invalidation + pre/post mutation abort (`styles/_engine/__tests__/invalidation.test.mjs`) [3h] {deps: T023}\n\n  Line 128: - [ ] T025 [P] Fixture: stale/absent FTS → source-scan `degraded:true` (`styles/_engine/__tests__/fallback.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T013}\n\n  Line 129: - [ ] T026 [P] Fixture: generation-mismatch hydration refusal (`styles/_engine/__tests__/hydrate-guard.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T018}\n\n  Line 130: - [ ] T027 [P] Fixture: deterministic card ordering + valid/invalid proof cards (`styles/_engine/__tests__/proof.test.mjs`) [2h] {deps: T014, T022}\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"(?:styles/_engine|_retrieval-manifest|CORPUS_USE_PROOF|retrieval substrate)","time":{"start":1784387028164,"end":1784387028175}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_049a62f6a112f532016a5b95d313648191a4de44e672b78280"}},"id":"prt_f75c14476001RVVy8hklTW9V7x","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c0fdba001mERY0fJtEb0OCQ"}}
