{"type":"text","timestamp":1784387131882,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"id":"prt_f75c2d6e1001zV821Nxr2FkpJD","messageID":"msg_f75c2a33d001XuwSCveodr6lAR","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","type":"text","text":"I’m writing iteration 4 as a write-once evidence packet and appending the matching canonical JSONL record. The delta also refreshes the older findings’ metadata so synthesis does not inherit the reducer’s earlier blank F001/F002 descriptions.","time":{"start":1784387131105,"end":1784387131880},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_062d5c043c3fe963016a5b963b131c819193f44a67c76a9d3f","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387286326,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_XoXW8gtT9y7m7Boz0dflOHhn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/review/lineages/sol-c/iterations/iteration-004.md\n+# Iteration 4: Maintainability and Handoff Safety\n+\n+## Dispatcher\n+\n+- Budget profile: verify\n+- Dimension: maintainability\n+- Prior active findings: F001-F003 (all P1)\n+- Search mode: graphless fallback using direct reads and exact packet-local searches\n+\n+## Files Reviewed\n+\n+- Phase 004 canonical documents: `004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `checklist.md`, `decision-record.md`, and `implementation-summary.md`\n+- Phase 004 path contract: `004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md:104-112`, `tasks.md:79-140`, and `decision-record.md:131-135,183,230,277,324`\n+- Packet-wide malformed-marker and placeholder searches across canonical Markdown documents\n+\n+## Findings - New\n+\n+### P0 Findings\n+\n+None.\n+\n+### P1 Findings\n+\n+None.\n+\n+### P2 Findings\n+\n+1. **Phase 004 canonical documents retain orphan transport closing tags** -- `.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md:283-284` -- All six phase-004 canonical documents end with an unmatched `</content>` token, and `spec.md` also ends with unmatched `</invoke>`. Exact packet-wide search found no corresponding opening tags and no such residue in the other implementation phases. The strict spec validator accepts these opaque lines, so they persist as rendered noise and can be mistaken for document structure by downstream extraction.\n+   - Finding class: artifact-hygiene\n+   - Scope proof: exact searches covered every Markdown file under the phase parent and located all seven malformed tokens only in phase 004.\n+   - Affected surface hints: phase 004 Markdown rendering, anchor extraction, routed context ingestion\n+   - Recommendation: remove the seven orphan transport tags and add a narrow malformed-wrapper check to document validation.\n+\n+2. **Phase 004 handoff truncates the task queue before two governance tasks** -- `.opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md:144-149` -- The implementation summary tells the next executor to implement T001-T028, while `tasks.md:139-140` defines T029 for one-ADR-per-module authority mapping and T030 for ADR promotion after validation. The summary separately mentions promotion but still presents the bounded task range as the implementation queue, making T029 easy to omit and leaving the handoff inconsistent with the authoritative task list.\n+   - Finding class: handoff-consistency\n+   - Scope proof: exact task-id search compared the only bounded T001-TNN handoff range with all task definitions in phase 004.\n+   - Affected surface hints: phase 004 resume handoff, ADR governance, task completion reconciliation\n+   - Recommendation: change the summary range to T001-T030 or avoid duplicating the task bounds and point to `tasks.md` as authoritative.\n+\n+## Findings - Refreshed\n+\n+- F001 remains P1: parent and completed research-child continuity still routes resume toward phase 001 instead of the phase-004 frontier.\n+- F002 remains P1: phase 006 still lacks an enforceable pre-prompt injection gate despite the upstream fixture requirement.\n+- F003 remains P1: six implementation checklist summary tables still disagree with their live P0/P1/P2 rows.\n+\n+## Candidate Search Ledger\n+\n+| ID | Bug class | Disposition | Evidence |\n+|----|-----------|-------------|----------|\n+| SL-008 | artifact_hygiene | finding F004 | phase 004 document endings and packet-wide exact search |\n+| SL-009 | queue_consistency | finding F005 | `implementation-summary.md:144-149`, `tasks.md:139-140` |\n+| SL-010 | path_precision | ruled out | `spec.md:104-112` and task file targets agree on proposed paths |\n+| SL-011 | authority_duplication | ruled out | plan summaries and ADR implementation paths preserve the same authority split |\n+\n+## Edge Cases\n+\n+- `TBD` verification dates in phases 009-010 are explicitly labeled planned-scaffold state, not unresolved implementation residue.\n+- Proposed engine paths do not exist yet by design; each is labeled NEW/proposed and is consistent across spec, plan, tasks, and ADRs.\n+- Repeated anti-slop and authority statements are deliberate invariant restatements, not conflicting definitions.\n+\n+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n+\n+- Phase 004 proposed file paths are internally consistent across its specification, plan, task queue, and ADR implementation sections.\n+- T001-T030 form a complete dependency queue; the defect is limited to the duplicated bounded range in the handoff summary.\n+- No malformed transport markers were found in implementation phases 005-010.\n+\n+## Next Focus\n+\n+- Dimension: stabilization\n+- Focus area: replay every active finding against current evidence and search for adjacent variants without opening a new scope.\n+- Reason: all configured dimensions now have evidence; legal convergence requires consecutive iterations without new P0/P1 findings.\n+- Required evidence: active-finding replay, exact adjacent-variant searches, candidate coverage, and final core-protocol status.\n+\n+## Verdict\n+\n+F001-F003 remain active P1 findings. F004-F005 are new P2 maintainability findings. No new P0/P1 finding was introduced.\n+\n+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/review/lineages/sol-c/deltas/iter-004.jsonl\n+{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"mode\":\"review\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\"run\":\"sol-c-004\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"maintainability and handoff safety\",\"dimensions\":[\"maintainability\"],\"filesReviewed\":[\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md:104-112,273-284\",\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/plan.md:325-354\",\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/tasks.md:79-169\",\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md:180-212\",\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/decision-record.md:300-333\",\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md:1-74,125-150\"],\"findingsCount\":5,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":3,\"P2\":2},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":2},\"findingsRefined\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"findingId\":\"F001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"category\":\"correctness\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"title\":\"Resume continuity points back to completed research\",\"file\":\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/spec.md\",\"line\":15,\"line_range\":\"15-16,46\",\"description\":\"Resume continuity still directs the operator to run phase 001 even though phases 001-003 are complete.\",\"evidence\":\"The parent and research-child continuity blocks identify completed research as the next action while phase 004 is the current frontier.\",\"recommendation\":\"Route continuity to phase 004 and preserve phases 001-003 as completed predecessors.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"lifecycle-state\",\"scopeProof\":\"Parent and all three completed research-child continuity blocks were compared with parent phase status and ordering.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"session resume\",\"phase routing\",\"parent continuity\"],\"content_hash\":\"c573671842aef0aa61fb93e6b7d0c7a43fc1f1320f1e48a356adfa6db64a50fd\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"findingId\":\"F002\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"category\":\"security\",\"dimension\":\"security\",\"title\":\"STUDY lacks an enforceable pre-prompt injection gate\",\"file\":\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/006-md-generator-study-exemplars/plan.md\",\"line\":83,\"line_range\":\"83-87,128-135\",\"description\":\"The STUDY plan names an injection envelope but does not define a pre-prompt rejection or neutralization gate with adversarial fixtures.\",\"evidence\":\"Phase-002 research requires embedded prompt-injection fixtures, while phase 006 covers authored-draft leakage but not hostile corpus instructions before prompt assembly.\",\"recommendation\":\"Specify the pre-prompt injection gate and adversarial fixtures before STUDY implementation.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\",\"scopeProof\":\"All phase 004-010 planning artifacts were searched for concrete prompt-injection controls.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"study hydration\",\"study transformer\",\"buildWritePrompt\",\"buildPlan\",\"runGuided\"],\"content_hash\":\"fcafdcafff36250dff8e257e1c6d0e13d629786af0b56f07f115302114e355ac\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"findingId\":\"F003\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"category\":\"traceability\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"title\":\"Verification Summary totals undercount checklist obligations\",\"file\":\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/checklist.md\",\"line\":127,\"line_range\":\"127-133\",\"description\":\"Six of seven implementation checklists publish verification-summary totals that do not equal their actual P0/P1/P2 checklist rows.\",\"evidence\":\"Exact priority-row counts disagree with summaries in phases 004 and 006-010; phase 005 is the matching control.\",\"recommendation\":\"Derive or mechanically validate every summary denominator from live checklist rows.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"matrix/evidence\",\"scopeProof\":\"Exact priority-row counts covered all seven implementation checklists.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"phase checklists\",\"completion reconciliation\",\"strict validation\"],\"content_hash\":\"e6025011ac3d86253aa4d633aa5887d01bd29c414da57797bd1bedfcb3ac3a13\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"findingId\":\"F004\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"category\":\"maintainability\",\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"title\":\"Phase 004 documents retain orphan transport tags\",\"file\":\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/spec.md\",\"line\":283,\"line_range\":\"283-284\",\"description\":\"All six phase-004 canonical documents end with unmatched </content>, and spec.md also ends with unmatched </invoke>.\",\"evidence\":\"Packet-wide exact search found seven closing transport tags, all in phase 004, with no corresponding opening tags.\",\"recommendation\":\"Remove the orphan tags and validate canonical documents for malformed wrapper residue.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"artifact-hygiene\",\"scopeProof\":\"Exact malformed-tag searches covered every Markdown file under the phase parent and localized all matches to phase 004.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"phase 004 Markdown rendering\",\"anchor extraction\",\"routed context ingestion\"],\"content_hash\":\"0ceb90d3104e2eaa2a0bd5f53ba022816036432ea983b4853e65e39ca85095b5\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"findingId\":\"F005\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"category\":\"maintainability\",\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"title\":\"Phase 004 handoff truncates the task queue at T028\",\"file\":\".opencode/specs/sk-design/011-sk-design-styles-utilization/004-retrieval-substrate/implementation-summary.md\",\"line\":146,\"line_range\":\"144-149\",\"description\":\"The handoff summary bounds implementation at T001-T028 although tasks.md defines governance tasks T029-T030.\",\"evidence\":\"The only bounded task range in the summary omits the task that maps modules to ADR authorities and the task that promotes validated ADRs.\",\"recommendation\":\"