ew/` directory on the first matching run and `{spec_folder}/review/{packet}-pt-{NN}/` only when prior non-matching content requires a separate packet), dispatch `@deep-review` agent per iteration, evaluate convergence across review dimensions, synthesize findings into `{artifact_dir}/review-report.md`, and emit `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md` at convergence unless `--no-resource-map` disables it. Use when auditing code, specs, skills, agents, or tracks for quality and release readiness.\n\n  Line 273: **Outputs:** Spec folder with `{artifact_dir}/` packet (flat-first `{spec_folder}/review/`, with `{spec_folder}/review/{packet}-pt-{NN}/` only for separated nested-phase packets), `review-report.md`, optional `resource-map.md`, state files, and `STATUS=<OK|FAIL|CANCELLED>`\n\n  Line 281: | Synth | Synthesize | Build finding registry, emit `review/resource-map.md`, deduplicate, compile `review/review-report.md` | `review/resource-map.md`, `review/review-report.md` (9 sections) |\n\n  Line 355: Artifacts: review/review-report.md, review/resource-map.md (unless `--no-resource-map`), [N] iteration files in review/, continuity update in canonical spec docs refreshed\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_confirm.yaml:\n  Line 93:   legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n\n  Line 109:   review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n\n  Line 142:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n\n  Line 144:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n\n  Line 280:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 386:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n\n  Line 663:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n\n  Line 1333:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 1334:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n\n  Line 1409:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n\n  Line 1470:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 sections and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n\n  Line 1472:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n  Line 1527:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"totalIterations\":{iteration_count},\"activeP0\":{active_p0},\"activeP1\":{active_p1},\"activeP2\":{active_p2},\"dimensionCoverage\":{dimension_coverage},\"verdict\":\"{verdict}\",\"releaseReadinessState\":\"{release_readiness_state}\",\"stopReason\":\"{reason}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n\n  Line 1538:         note: \"Skill-owned contract fix (028): without this stage step, operators who do `git add review-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal — log warning and continue.\"\n\n  Line 1544:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n\n  Line 1548:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n\n  Line 1558:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n\n  Line 1605:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_research_confirm.yaml:\n  Line 171:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n\n  Line 173:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n\n  Line 594:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n\n  Line 1159:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 1274:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"totalIterations\":{iteration_count},\"answeredCount\":{answered_count},\"totalQuestions\":{total_questions},\"stopReason\":\"{reason}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_agent-improvement_confirm.yaml:\n  Line 280:       step_emit_journal_event_legal_stop_evaluated:\n\n  Line 281:         description: \"Emit legal_stop_evaluated journal event with all five gate bundles after the operator gate is evaluated\"\n\n  Line 282:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit legal_stop_evaluated --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":\\\"{iteration}\\\",\\\"gateResults\\\":{\\\"contractGate\\\":\\\"{contract_gate}\\\",\\\"behaviorGate\\\":\\\"{behavior_gate}\\\",\\\"integrationGate\\\":\\\"{integration_gate}\\\",\\\"evidenceGate\\\":\\\"{evidence_gate}\\\",\\\"improvementGate\\\":\\\"{improvement_gate}\\\"},\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"{stop_reason}\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 292:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_alignment_confirm.yaml:\n  Line 188:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 396:         if_converged: { proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n\n  Line 397:         if_stop_max_iterations: { log: \"Max iterations ({max_iterations}) reached without full convergence; proceeding to synthesis with current coverage/stability as recorded evidence.\", proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n\n  Line 398:         if_nothing_to_converge: { log: \"Zero applicable lanes -- nothing to converge. Proceeding to synthesis.\", proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n\n  Line 404:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_agent-improvement_presentation.txt:\n  Line 449: - **Legal-stop emission** (post-060/005): YAML emits nested `legal_stop_evaluated.details.gateResults.{contractGate,behaviorGate,integrationGate,evidenceGate,improvementGate}` matching the reducer consumer shape. Flat `gateResult/gateName` is retired.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_review.body.md:\n  Line 124: The YAML workflow runs iterative code review by initializing a review packet under `{artifact_dir}`, dispatching fresh deep-review LEAF agents, evaluating convergence across configured review dimensions, and synthesizing findings into `review-report.md` plus optional `resource-map.md`. Convergence uses the review-specific `convergenceThreshold` severity-weighted finding ratio; do not transfer sibling defaults from deep-research or deep-ai-council. Code graph tool IDs remain stable as `code_graph_query` and `code_graph_context`; implementation and docs live under `.opencode/skills/system-code-graph/`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_model-benchmark_auto.yaml:\n  Line 182:       step_emit_journal_event_legal_stop_evaluated:\n\n  Line 183:         description: \"Emit legal_stop_evaluated journal event after stop-condition evaluation\"\n\n  Line 184:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit legal_stop_evaluated --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":\\\"{iteration}\\\",\\\"scoringMethod\\\":\\\"{scoring_method}\\\",\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"{stop_reason}\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 186:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep_review.contract.md:\n  Line 353:    - `\"Review review/review-report.md contract drift, E, all, A, 7, 0.10, B, gpt-5.4, high, fast\"`\n","metadata":{"matches":86,"truncated":false},"title":"step_emit_blocked_stop|synthesis_complete|phase_synthesis|review-report\\.md|legal_stop|releaseReadinessState","time":{"start":1784387580817,"end":1784387580843}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca2148191bdd4c992bbc520aa"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b329001JF4sU6D2YrBSmC","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387580861,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ihMzy4LMCOPBhSzJAo07IFVa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","offset":90,"limit":95},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n90: \n91: Every terminal stop and every blocked-stop vote MUST emit the shared stop contract from REQ-001: a named `stopReason` enum plus, when STOP is vetoed, a `blocked_stop` event written to `deep-review-state.jsonl`. There is no nested `legalStop` wrapper on the persisted path. Earlier drafts of this document implied one, and that drift was the source of F009 in the 042 closing audit.\n92: \n93: ### Convergence Modes\n94: \n95: The shared convergence runtime accepts four values. Review legality, security gates, target authority, and verdict derivation remain owned by the review workflow rather than the convergence mode.\n96: \n97: | Mode | Live Behavior |\n98: |------|---------------|\n99: | `default` | Uses normal full-history convergence signals and sends a legal STOP to synthesis and verdict derivation. This is the fallback when no mode is supplied. |\n100: | `off` | Is accepted and persisted, but the shipped review YAML has no `off` decision branch; review therefore follows the same legal-stop and synthesis path as `default`. Use `stopPolicy: \"max-iterations\"` when convergence must remain telemetry-only until the iteration ceiling. |\n101: | `sliding-window` | Is accepted and persisted, but windowed graph-novelty telemetry is research-only in the shared runtime; review therefore retains its ordinary full-history signals, legal-stop gates, and synthesis path. |\n102: | `divergent` | After all review gates pass, translates the eligible `all_dimensions_clean` STOP into a read-only three-seat direction-selection pivot and continues with the selected review direction. |\n103: \n104: #### Divergent Pivot Contract\n105: \n106: Review has one eligible reason: the exact internal reason `all_dimensions_clean` with decision `STOP`. The nine legal-stop gates run before the divergent branch and remain unchanged. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, unrecoverable error, and any blocked security or quality gate therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.\n107: \n108: Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n109: \n110: The guarantees are absolute: divergent mode never changes the PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL mapping, never authorizes a fix, and never makes the review target writable. A successful pivot returns to the loop before `phase_synthesis`; verdict computation exists only inside `phase_synthesis`, where active P0 yields FAIL, active P1 yields CONDITIONAL, and no active P0/P1 yields PASS. A failed pivot fails closed to that existing synthesis path.\n111: \n112: Every pivot dispatches three seats, so a run that pivots has proportionally higher model cost and duration than the same run under `default`, `off`, or `sliding-window`. Pivot evidence is isolated under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, including config, append-only state, three seat artifacts, deliberation, and report. This path is distinct from ordinary planning Council artifacts under a spec packet's `ai-council/**` tree.\n113: \n114: #### stopReason Enum\n115: \n116: | `stopReason` | Meaning |\n117: |--------------|---------|\n118: | `converged` | All convergence signals met and legal-stop gates passed. |\n119: | `maxIterationsReached` | Iteration limit hit before convergence. |\n120: | `userPaused` | User requested pause via sentinel. |\n121: | `blockedStop` | Convergence math voted stop but legal-stop gates failed. |\n122: | `stuckRecovery` | Stuck detection triggered recovery. |\n123: | `error` | Unrecoverable error during iteration or reducer flow. |\n124: | `manualStop` | Operator explicitly halted outside the pause sentinel path. |\n125: \n126: #### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n127: \n128: `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n129: \n130: ```json\n131: {\n132:   \"type\": \"event\",\n133:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n134:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n135:   \"run\": 5,\n136:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n137:   \"gateResults\": {\n138:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n139:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n140:       \"pass\": false,\n141:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n142:       \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n143:     },\n144:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n145:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n146:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n147:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n148:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n149:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n150:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n151:   },\n152:   \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n153:   \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n154:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n155:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n156:   \"generation\": 1\n157: }\n158: ```\n159: \n160: - `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n161: - `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n162: - `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n163: - `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.\n164: - When the graph convergence verdict is `STOP_BLOCKED`, fold the graph blocker gate name into `blockedBy` and preserve the structured blocker objects under `graphBlockerDetail`.\n165: \n166: ### Decision Priority\n167: \n168: Checks are evaluated in this order (first match wins):\n169: \n170: 1. **Max iterations** -- hard cap, always checked first.\n171: 2. **All dimensions covered + clean** -- all 4 dimensions covered, no active P0/P1, stabilization passed, gates passed.\n172: 3. **Stuck detection** -- 2+ consecutive no-progress iterations.\n173: 4. **Composite convergence** -- 3-signal weighted vote with threshold 0.60.\n174: 5. **Legal-stop gate bundle** -- review-specific stop gates. If a stop vote fails any gate, persist `stopReason=blockedStop` and continue.\n175: 6. **Default CONTINUE** -- none of the above triggered.\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: ## 2. HARD STOPS\n180: \n181: Hard stops are evaluated first and override all other signals.\n182: \n183: ### Max Iterations Reached\n184: \n\n(Showing lines 90-184 of 606. Use offset=185 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\nEvery terminal stop and every blocked-stop vote MUST emit the shared stop contract from REQ-001: a named `stopReason` enum plus, when STOP is vetoed, a `blocked_stop` event written to `deep-review-state.jsonl`. There is no nested `legalStop` wrapper on the persisted path. Earlier drafts of this document implied one, and that drift was the source of F009 in the 042 closing audit.\n\n### Convergence Modes\n\nThe shared convergence runtime accepts four values. Review legality, security gates, target authority, and verdict derivation remain owned by the review workflow rather than the convergence mode.\n\n| Mode | Live Behavior |\n|------|---------------|\n| `default` | Uses normal full-history convergence signals and sends a legal STOP to synthesis and verdict derivation. This is the fallback when no mode is supplied. |\n| `off` | Is accepted and persisted, but the shipped review YAML has no `off` decision branch; review therefore follows the same legal-stop and synthesis path as `default`. Use `stopPolicy: \"max-iterations\"` when convergence must remain telemetry-only until the iteration ceiling. |\n| `sliding-window` | Is accepted and persisted, but windowed graph-novelty telemetry is research-only in the shared runtime; review therefore retains its ordinary full-history signals, legal-stop gates, and synthesis path. |\n| `divergent` | After all review gates pass, translates the eligible `all_dimensions_clean` STOP into a read-only three-seat direction-selection pivot and continues with the selected review direction. |\n\n#### Divergent Pivot Contract\n\nReview has one eligible reason: the exact internal reason `all_dimensions_clean` with decision `STOP`. The nine legal-stop gates run before the divergent branch and remain unchanged. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, unrecoverable error, and any blocked security or quality gate therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.\n\nEach eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","text":"\nEvery terminal stop and every blocked-stop vote MUST emit the shared stop contract from REQ-001: a named `stopReason` enum plus, when STOP is vetoed, a `blocked_stop` event written to `deep-review-state.jsonl`. There is no nested `legalStop` wrapper on the persisted path. Earlier drafts of this document implied one, and that drift was the source of F009 in the 042 closing audit.\n\n### Convergence Modes\n\nThe shared convergence runtime accepts four values. Review legality, security gates, target authority, and verdict derivation remain owned by the review workflow rather than the convergence mode.\n\n| Mode | Live Behavior |\n|------|---------------|\n| `default` | Uses normal full-history convergence signals and sends a legal STOP to synthesis and verdict derivation. This is the fallback when no mode is supplied. |\n| `off` | Is accepted and persisted, but the shipped review YAML has no `off` decision branch; review therefore follows the same legal-stop and synthesis path as `default`. Use `stopPolicy: \"max-iterations\"` when convergence must remain telemetry-only until the iteration ceiling. |\n| `sliding-window` | Is accepted and persisted, but windowed graph-novelty telemetry is research-only in the shared runtime; review therefore retains its ordinary full-history signals, legal-stop gates, and synthesis path. |\n| `divergent` | After all review gates pass, translates the eligible `all_dimensions_clean` STOP into a read-only three-seat direction-selection pivot and continues with the selected review direction. |\n\n#### Divergent Pivot Contract\n\nReview has one eligible reason: the exact internal reason `all_dimensions_clean` with decision `STOP`. The nine legal-stop gates run before the divergent branch and remain unchanged. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, unrecoverable error, and any blocked security or quality gate therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.\n\nEach eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n\nThe guarantees are absolute: divergent mode never changes the PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL mapping, never authorizes a fix, and never makes the review target writable. A successful pivot returns to the loop before `phase_synthesis`; verdict computation exists only inside `phase_synthesis`, where active P0 yields FAIL, active P1 yields CONDITIONAL, and no active P0/P1 yields PASS. A failed pivot fails closed to that existing synthesis path.\n\nEvery pivot dispatches three seats, so a run that pivots has proportionally higher model cost and duration than the same run under `default`, `off`, or `sliding-window`. Pivot evidence is isolated under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, including config, append-only state, three seat artifacts, deliberation, and report. This path is distinct from ordinary planning Council artifacts under a spec packet's `ai-council/**` tree.\n\n#### stopReason Enum\n\n| `stopReason` | Meaning |\n|--------------|---------|\n| `converged` | All convergence signals met and legal-stop gates passed. |\n| `maxIterationsReached` | Iteration limit hit before convergence. |\n| `userPaused` | User requested pause via sentinel. |\n| `blockedStop` | Convergence math voted stop but legal-stop gates failed. |\n| `stuckRecovery` | Stuck detection triggered recovery. |\n| `error` | Unrecoverable error during iteration or reducer flow. |\n| `manualStop` | Operator explicitly halted outside the pause sentinel path. |\n\n#### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n\n`step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 5,\n  \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n  \"gateResults\": {\n    \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n    \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n      \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n    },\n    \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n    \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n    \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n    \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n    \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n    \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n    \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n  },\n  \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n  \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n- `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n- `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n- `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.\n- When the graph convergence verdict is `STOP_BLOCKED`, fold the graph blocker gate name into `blockedBy` and preserve the structured blocker objects under `graphBlockerDetail`.\n\n### Decision Priority\n\nChecks are evaluated in this order (first match wins):\n\n1. **Max iterations** -- hard cap, always checked first.\n2. **All dimensions covered + clean** -- all 4 dimensions covered, no active P0/P1, stabilization passed, gates passed.\n3. **Stuck detection** -- 2+ consecutive no-progress iterations.\n4. **Composite convergence** -- 3-signal weighted vote with threshold 0.60.\n5. **Legal-stop gate bundle** -- review-specific stop gates. If a stop vote fails any gate, persist `stopReason=blockedStop` and continue.\n6. **Default CONTINUE** -- none of the above triggered.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HARD STOPS\n\nHard stops are evaluated first and override all other signals.\n\n### Max Iterations Reached\n","lineStart":90,"lineEnd":184,"totalLines":606,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","time":{"start":1784387580837,"end":1784387580858}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca2348191a00aa3314e0b7efd"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b397001ExzQLZEW2r6RYF","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387580864,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OM2VLJhfkc887sNmmH50UL2K","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion_criteria.md","offset":1,"limit":160},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion_criteria.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Completion Criteria\n3: description: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n6:   - \"review success criteria\"\n7:   - \"review definition of done\"\n8:   - \"review release readiness validation\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Completion Criteria\n15: \n16: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: This reference is the authoritative checklist for \"is this review loop actually done.\" SKILL.md §6 SUCCESS CRITERIA carries a condensed summary and links here for the full enumeration; use this file when verifying a completed run, debugging a premature STOP, or reconciling completion metadata against the loop's real state.\n25: \n26: ### When to Use\n27: \n28: - Verifying a review loop's completion before accepting its verdict.\n29: - Debugging why STOP was blocked or why synthesis produced an incomplete report.\n30: - Reconciling `review-report.md` claims against the canonical state files.\n31: - Auditing a run for the release-readiness handoff.\n32: \n33: ### Relationship to `loop_state_and_gates.md`\n34: \n35: `references/protocol/loop_state_and_gates.md` defines the three state-machine-level binary gates (Evidence, Scope, Coverage) that block a STOP *decision* inside the convergence check. This file is the broader definition-of-done: it also covers artifact existence, report structure, severity-field completeness, and the release-readiness handoff -- checked once the loop believes it has already reached STOP.\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 2. LOOP COMPLETION\n40: \n41: A review loop is considered complete when every item below holds:\n42: \n43: - The loop reached convergence (composite stop score above `compositeStopScore`, with required gates green) OR hit `maxIterations` without false-positive STOP.\n44: - Every configured review dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage recorded in `deep-review-state.jsonl` and reflected in `deep-review-strategy.md`.\n45: - Required traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) executed at least once. Overlay protocols that apply to the target type ran or were explicitly marked N/A.\n46: - All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n47: - `review/resource-map.md` was emitted from converged delta evidence unless `config.resource_map.emit == false` (operator flag `--no-resource-map`).\n48: - `review/review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections (Executive Summary, Planning Trigger, Active Finding Registry, Remediation Workstreams, Spec Seed, Plan Seed, Traceability Status, Deferred Items, Audit Appendix) plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present == true`.\n49: - Canonical continuity surfaces updated via `generate-context.js` (description.json, graph-metadata.json, indexed memory entries).\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. QUALITY GATES\n54: \n55: Each gate is binary: pass or block. STOP cannot be legal until every gate passes.\n56: \n57: - **Config validity**: `deep-review-config.json` parses, names every required field, and lineage block matches the current run (`sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, `releaseReadinessState`).\n58: - **Strategy initialization**: `deep-review-strategy.md` carries the Files Under Review table, Cross-Reference Status grouped by core vs overlay, Known Context, and Review Boundaries.\n59: - **State consistency**: `deep-review-state.jsonl` opens with the config record and appends one iteration record per dispatched iteration. Reducer-owned fields in `deep-review-findings-registry.json` reconcile against JSONL totals.\n60: - **Iteration completeness**: every dispatched iteration produced both an `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` (non-empty, ending with the canonical `Review verdict: PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` line) AND a JSONL delta record with `findingDetails[]`, `findingsSummary`, `newFindingsRatio`.\n61: - **Severity coverage**: every reported finding carries `severity` in {P0, P1, P2}, `category`, `file:line` evidence, `finding_class`, and a `content_hash` for synthesis dedup.\n62: - **Advisory numeric score**: `riskScore` may appear in finding details as non-gating context only; verdict logic must ignore it.\n63: - **Adversarial replay**: every P0 finding survived adversarial self-check. Rejected P0s downgraded with rationale recorded in the iteration narrative.\n64: - **Coverage threshold**: `dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count` AND required traceability protocols covered, stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations.\n65: - **Acceptance coverage**: when the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is active, the final report records `AC_COVERAGE` status, covered/total, floor, and next action; default-off INFO output is advisory and does not by itself block STOP.\n66: - **Security-sensitive override**: when the run targets security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, or shared policy, the gates from `references/convergence/convergence.md` \"Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\" apply (`minStabilizationPasses=2`, closed-finding replay required, fix-completeness gate enforced).\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 4. VALIDATION SUCCESS\n71: \n72: The release-readiness handoff is valid when:\n73: \n74: - The final report records stop reason, iteration count, dimension coverage, severity counts (P0/P1/P2), verdict (PASS / CONDITIONAL / FAIL), and release-readiness state (`in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking`).\n75: - Verdict logic matches: PASS = no P0/P1 findings (P2 advisories permitted with `hasAdvisories: true`). CONDITIONAL = P1 findings present with remediation plan. FAIL = any P0 confirmed after adversarial self-check.\n76: - `resource-map.md` Phase-5 Augmentation section (if present) lists novel logic gaps with iteration source links, or explicitly records the empty-result case.\n77: - `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` still surfaces the skill after any graph-metadata edits.\n78: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` exits 0 on the target spec folder.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n83: \n84: - `references/protocol/loop_state_and_gates.md` -- state transitions, error handling, and the Evidence/Scope/Coverage STOP-decision gates.\n85: - `references/state/state_outputs.md` -- packet file ownership and the `review-report.md` section list.\n86: - `references/state/state_format.md` -- schemas for every state file referenced above.\n87: - `references/convergence/convergence.md` -- composite stop score, `minStabilizationPasses`, and Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides.\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Completion Criteria\ndescription: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n  - \"review success criteria\"\n  - \"review definition of done\"\n  - \"review release readiness validation\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Completion Criteria\n\nFull definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion_criteria.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Completion Criteria\ndescription: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n  - \"review success criteria\"\n  - \"review definition of done\"\n  - \"review release readiness validation\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Completion Criteria\n\nFull definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis reference is the authoritative checklist for \"is this review loop actually done.\" SKILL.md §6 SUCCESS CRITERIA carries a condensed summary and links here for the full enumeration; use this file when verifying a completed run, debugging a premature STOP, or reconciling completion metadata against the loop's real state.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Verifying a review loop's completion before accepting its verdict.\n- Debugging why STOP was blocked or why synthesis produced an incomplete report.\n- Reconciling `review-report.md` claims against the canonical state files.\n- Auditing a run for the release-readiness handoff.\n\n### Relationship to `loop_state_and_gates.md`\n\n`references/protocol/loop_state_and_gates.md` defines the three state-machine-level binary gates (Evidence, Scope, Coverage) that block a STOP *decision* inside the convergence check. This file is the broader definition-of-done: it also covers artifact existence, report structure, severity-field completeness, and the release-readiness handoff -- checked once the loop believes it has already reached STOP.\n\n---\n\n## 2. LOOP COMPLETION\n\nA review loop is considered complete when every item below holds:\n\n- The loop reached convergence (composite stop score above `compositeStopScore`, with required gates green) OR hit `maxIterations` without false-positive STOP.\n- Every configured review dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage recorded in `deep-review-state.jsonl` and reflected in `deep-review-strategy.md`.\n- Required traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) executed at least once. Overlay protocols that apply to the target type ran or were explicitly marked N/A.\n- All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n- `review/resource-map.md` was emitted from converged delta evidence unless `config.resource_map.emit == false` (operator flag `--no-resource-map`).\n- `review/review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections (Executive Summary, Planning Trigger, Active Finding Registry, Remediation Workstreams, Spec Seed, Plan Seed, Traceability Status, Deferred Items, Audit Appendix) plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present == true`.\n- Canonical continuity surfaces updated via `generate-context.js` (description.json, graph-metadata.json, indexed memory entries).\n\n---\n\n## 3. QUALITY GATES\n\nEach gate is binary: pass or block. STOP cannot be legal until every gate passes.\n\n- **Config validity**: `deep-review-config.json` parses, names every required field, and lineage block matches the current run (`sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, `releaseReadinessState`).\n- **Strategy initialization**: `deep-review-strategy.md` carries the Files Under Review table, Cross-Reference Status grouped by core vs overlay, Known Context, and Review Boundaries.\n- **State consistency**: `deep-review-state.jsonl` opens with the config record and appends one iteration record per dispatched iteration. Reducer-owned fields in `deep-review-findings-registry.json` reconcile against JSONL totals.\n- **Iteration completeness**: every dispatched iteration produced both an `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` (non-empty, ending with the canonical `Review verdict: PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` line) AND a JSONL delta record with `findingDetails[]`, `findingsSummary`, `newFindingsRatio`.\n- **Severity coverage**: every reported finding carries `severity` in {P0, P1, P2}, `category`, `file:line` evidence, `finding_class`, and a `content_hash` for synthesis dedup.\n- **Advisory numeric score**: `riskScore` may appear in finding details as non-gating context only; verdict logic must ignore it.\n- **Adversarial replay**: every P0 finding survived adversarial self-check. Rejected P0s downgraded with rationale recorded in the iteration narrative.\n- **Coverage threshold**: `dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count` AND required traceability protocols covered, stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations.\n- **Acceptance coverage**: when the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is active, the final report records `AC_COVERAGE` status, covered/total, floor, and next action; default-off INFO output is advisory and does not by itself block STOP.\n- **Security-sensitive override**: when the run targets security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, or shared policy, the gates from `references/convergence/convergence.md` \"Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\" apply (`minStabilizationPasses=2`, closed-finding replay required, fix-completeness gate enforced).\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION SUCCESS\n\nThe release-readiness handoff is valid when:\n\n- The final report records stop reason, iteration count, dimension coverage, severity counts (P0/P1/P2), verdict (PASS / CONDITIONAL / FAIL), and release-readiness state (`in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking`).\n- Verdict logic matches: PASS = no P0/P1 findings (P2 advisories permitted with `hasAdvisories: true`). CONDITIONAL = P1 findings present with remediation plan. FAIL = any P0 confirmed after adversarial self-check.\n- `resource-map.md` Phase-5 Augmentation section (if present) lists novel logic gaps with iteration source links, or explicitly records the empty-result case.\n- `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` still surfaces the skill after any graph-metadata edits.\n- `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` exits 0 on the target spec folder.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/protocol/loop_state_and_gates.md` -- state transitions, error handling, and the Evidence/Scope/Coverage STOP-decision gates.\n- `references/state/state_outputs.md` -- packet file ownership and the `review-report.md` section list.\n- `references/state/state_format.md` -- schemas for every state file referenced above.\n- `references/convergence/convergence.md` -- composite stop score, `minStabilizationPasses`, and Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion_criteria.md","time":{"start":1784387580852,"end":1784387580862}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca23c819192938616218d45ad"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b3a7001TMb7QJlfBzBxux","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387580936,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_rBUM4GZZtHmOoKQPLrSNcYRi","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"verify.*artifact|verify.*review|review-report|synthesis_complete|resource-map","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts","include":"*.cjs"},"output":"Found 16 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs:\n  Line 123: function verify(loopType, artifactDir, iteration) {\n\n  Line 178:     process.stdout.write('Usage: verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type review|research|context|alignment --artifact-dir <dir> --iteration <N> [--json]\\n');\n\n  Line 186:   const result = verify(args.loopType, args.artifactDir, args.iteration);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:\n  Line 13: const { emitResourceMap } = require('../../shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs');\n\n  Line 168:         `[deep-review] resource-map extractor skipped ${corruptionWarnings.length} malformed delta row(s) from ${fileName}`,\n\n  Line 438:     if (record.event === 'synthesis_complete') {\n\n  Line 484:     } else if (record.event === 'resumed' || record.event === 'restarted' || record.event === 'synthesis_complete') {\n\n  Line 1465:     if (record.type === 'iteration' || record.event === 'synthesis_complete') {\n\n  Line 2047:   const resourceMapPath = path.join(reviewDir, 'resource-map.md');\n\n  Line 2077:   // rows first while the resource-map emit path reuses the same parsed data.\n\n  Line 2163:   const emitResourceMapOutput = args.includes('--emit-resource-map');\n\n  Line 2171:       'Usage: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder> [--artifact-dir <path>] [--lenient] [--create-missing-anchors] [--emit-resource-map]\\n',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:\n  Line 551:   if (loopType === 'review') return [path.join(lineageDir, 'review-report.md')];\n\n  Line 628:     .find((record) => record && record.type === 'event' && record.event === 'synthesis_complete');\n\n  Line 630:     return 'missing synthesis_complete event for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n\n  Line 1730:       // deep-review-state.jsonl, review-report.md, resource-map.md) INTO lineageDir, so a\n","metadata":{"matches":16,"truncated":false},"title":"verify.*artifact|verify.*review|review-report|synthesis_complete|resource-map","time":{"start":1784387580909,"end":1784387580927}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca24481919e3a796d64767604"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b3d9001UazRGObUT1B96v","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387581228,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_c8hSN3YlJ4AdleWpUtJDTYOj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/*report*","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"No files found","metadata":{"count":0,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1784387580919,"end":1784387581226}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca24c8191bfb976a564ef08ef"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b3f00012eF6qz0CAuRaq6","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387581231,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_ADMpuMhrb78tvwaHMKUmKnXD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/**/*resource*map*.md","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/command_flow_stress_tests/resource_map_coverage_gate.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/synthesis_save_and_guardrails/resource_map_emission.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature_catalog/loop_lifecycle/resource_map_coverage_gate.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature_catalog/loop_lifecycle/resource_map_emission.md","metadata":{"count":4,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1784387580923,"end":1784387581229}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_062c0aa37d483845016a5b97fca254819182004da99f60a22d"}},"id":"prt_f75c9b3f9001z4i4lYf6YcrZyN","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1784387582636,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"id":"prt_f75c9baa9001vic5MGSiZPM1A6","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_f75c984910015Fd4p8uf9l8Fa1","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":128813,"input":839,"output":441,"reasoning":45,"cache":{"write":0,"read":127488}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1784387588977,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"id":"prt_f75c9d36f001YPrThWqmLzK8KQ","messageID":"msg_f75c9c057001vYQnpmVsQIkzpJ","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387593887,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8Hvh2nMMHcBQ2rF5N3cubgs5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","offset":600,"limit":175},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n600:           4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n601:                signals = []\n602:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n603:                   avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n604:                   stop if avg <= 0.08\n605:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n606:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n607:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n608:                c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n609:                   coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n610:                   stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n611:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n612:                if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n613:                if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n614:                else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n615:           5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n616:                a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n617:                b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n618:                c) p0ResolutionGate: pass when activeP0 == 0; record activeP0\n619:                d) evidenceDensityGate: pass when every active P0/P1 has concrete file:line evidence and no active P0/P1 relies only on inference; record avgEvidencePerFinding\n620:                e) hotspotSaturationGate: pass when review hotspots have been revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic\n621:                f) claimAdjudicationGate: pass when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == true (i.e. last_claim_adjudication_passed != false OR there are no active P0/P1 findings to adjudicate); record last_claim_adjudication_passed and claim_adjudication_active_count\n622:                g) fixCompletenessReplayGate: pass when security_sensitive_fix_scope == false OR every required closed-gate replay row passes with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage; record security_sensitive_fix_scope, fix_completeness_replay_required_rows, and fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows\n623:                h) candidateCoverageGate: skip entirely when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 on the latest iteration. Otherwise pass when the current iteration's `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass` is `trivial` with `enforcement: \"skip\"` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` is non-empty, OR when the reducer registry's `searchDebt` is empty AND `candidateCoverage.covered` is a superset of `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` for the lineage. Otherwise pass = false; record `searchDebt` items as blocked-stop evidence; blocker name = \"candidateCoverageGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Resolve deferred/blocked obligations in next iteration or downgrade scope explicitly to trivial with cited evidence.\"\n624:                i) graphlessFallbackGate: skip when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 OR the reducer registry's last-iteration `searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode` is `graph`. Applies when graphCoverageMode is `graphless_fallback` or `unavailable_blocked`. Pass when graphCoverageMode is `graphless_fallback` AND at least one `searchLedger` row exists for each entry in `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` with `searchActions[].method` in {\"direct_read\",\"exact_grep\",\"semantic_search\",\"code_graph_status_check\",\"producer_consumer_trace\",\"negative_test_inspection\"} AND non-empty `evidenceRefs`. Fail automatically when graphCoverageMode is `unavailable_blocked`; record the explicit unavailability reason. Otherwise pass = false; blocker name = \"graphlessFallbackGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Add cited fallback ledger rows (direct read, exact search, producer/consumer trace, negative-test inspection) or set graphCoverageMode to 'graph' once graph data is available.\"\n625:              if STOP is a candidate and any gate fails:\n626:                decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n627:                stop_blocked = true\n628:                stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n629:                blocked_by_json = JSON array of failing gate names (always include \"claimAdjudicationGate\" when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false, \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\" when fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass == false, \"candidateCoverageGate\" when candidate_coverage_gate_pass == false, and \"graphlessFallbackGate\" when graphless_fallback_gate_pass == false)\n630:                blocked_by_csv = comma-separated list of failing gate names\n631:                convergence_gate_pass = boolean\n632:                convergence_gate_score = numeric convergence score\n633:                dimension_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n634:                dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = JSON array of covered review dimensions\n635:                dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = JSON array of missing review dimensions\n636:                p0_resolution_gate_pass = boolean\n637:                active_p0_count = number of active P0 findings\n638:                evidence_density_gate_pass = boolean\n639:                avg_evidence_per_finding = numeric evidence density\n640:                hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = boolean\n641:                claim_adjudication_gate_pass = boolean\n642:                claim_adjudication_active_count = numeric count of active P0/P1 at the gate\n643:                fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = boolean\n644:                security_sensitive_fix_scope = boolean\n645:                fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = numeric count of closed-gate replay rows required for security-sensitive fix reruns\n646:                fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = numeric count of required closed-gate replay rows marked PASS with evidence\n647:                candidate_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n648:                candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations blocking STOP, else []\n649:                candidate_coverage_missing_json = JSON array of required bug classes not present in candidateCoverage.covered, else []\n650:                graphless_fallback_gate_pass = boolean\n651:                graphless_fallback_mode = latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\n652:                graphless_fallback_missing_json = JSON array of required bug classes without cited fallback ledger rows, else []\n653:                graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = explicit reason when graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n654:                recovery_strategy = one-line hint describing the next review action needed to satisfy the failed gates; combine candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate recovery guidance when both fail (when claimAdjudicationGate is the failing gate, prefer the step-0 recovery_strategy already set)\n655:           6. COMBINED STOP RULE:\n656:                a) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\": decision = \"STOP\"\n657:                b) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n658:                     decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n659:                     stop_blocked = true\n660:                     stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n661:                     # Blocked-stop closure: blockedBy must be string[] per the\n662:                     # published review blocked-stop contract. Extract the `.type`\n663:                     # field from each structured graph blocker; preserve the full\n664:                     # objects in graph_blocker_detail_json for operator inspection.\n665:                     blocked_by_json = JSON.stringify(graph_blockers_json.map(b => typeof b === \"string\" ? b : (b && b.type) || \"graph_blocker\"))\n666:                     blocked_by_csv = graph_blockers_csv\n667:                     graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n668:                     recovery_strategy = \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\"\n669:                c) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"CONTINUE\":\n670:                     decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n671:                     stop_blocked = false\n672:                     reason = \"graph_convergence_continue\"\n673:                d) else keep the existing STUCK_RECOVERY or CONTINUE outcome\n674:         outputs:\n675:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n676:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n677:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n678:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n679:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n680:           - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n681:           - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n682:           - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n683:           - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n684:           - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n685:           - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n686:           - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n687:           - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n688:           - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n689:           - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n690:           - claim_adjudication_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for claimAdjudicationGate (false vetoes STOP)\"\n691:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings evaluated by claimAdjudicationGate\"\n692:           - fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for fixCompletenessReplayGate (false vetoes STOP on security-sensitive fix reruns)\"\n693:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the review is a security-sensitive fix rerun\"\n694:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count of closed-gate replay rows required before STOP\"\n695:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count of required closed-gate replay rows that passed with evidence\"\n696:           - candidate_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for candidateCoverageGate (false vetoes STOP for unresolved reducer-owned search debt or uncovered required bug classes)\"\n697:           - candidate_coverage_search_debt_json: \"JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations used as blocked-stop evidence\"\n698:           - candidate_coverage_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing from candidateCoverage.covered\"\n699:           - graphless_fallback_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for graphlessFallbackGate (false vetoes STOP when graphless fallback evidence is absent or unavailable_blocked)\"\n700:           - graphless_fallback_mode: \"Latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\"\n701:           - graphless_fallback_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing cited fallback ledger rows\"\n702:           - graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason: \"Explicit unavailability reason when graphCoverageMode == unavailable_blocked\"\n703:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED from step_graph_convergence\"\n704:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by graph convergence\"\n705:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers\"\n706:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker summary\"\n707:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next review action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n708: \n709:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n710:         action: \"Persist blocked-stop evidence whenever the review legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP\"\n711:         if_blocked:\n712:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergenceGate\":{\"pass\":{convergence_gate_pass},\"score\":{convergence_gate_score}},\"dimensionCoverageGate\":{\"pass\":{dimension_coverage_gate_pass},\"covered\":{dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json},\"missing\":{dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json}},\"p0ResolutionGate\":{\"pass\":{p0_resolution_gate_pass},\"activeP0\":{active_p0_count}},\"evidenceDensityGate\":{\"pass\":{evidence_density_gate_pass},\"avgEvidencePerFinding\":{avg_evidence_per_finding}},\"hotspotSaturationGate\":{\"pass\":{hotspot_saturation_gate_pass}},\"claimAdjudicationGate\":{\"pass\":{claim_adjudication_gate_pass},\"activeP0P1\":{claim_adjudication_active_count}},\"fixCompletenessReplayGate\":{\"pass\":{fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass},\"securitySensitive\":{security_sensitive_fix_scope},\"requiredRows\":{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows},\"passingRows\":{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}},\"candidateCoverageGate\":{\"pass\":{candidate_coverage_gate_pass},\"searchDebt\":{candidate_coverage_search_debt_json},\"missing\":{candidate_coverage_missing_json}},\"graphlessFallbackGate\":{\"pass\":{graphless_fallback_gate_pass},\"mode\":\"{graphless_fallback_mode}\",\"missing\":{graphless_fallback_missing_json},\"unavailabilityReason\":\"{graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason}\"}},\"graphBlockerDetail\":{graph_blockers_json},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n713:           log: \"Blocked STOP persisted for review loop. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n714:         if_not_blocked:\n715:           proceed: true\n716: \n717:       step_handle_convergence:\n718:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n719:         if_stop:\n720:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n721:           if_divergent_eligible:\n722:             eligibility_contract:\n723:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n724:               eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n725:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n726:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n727:             steps:\n728:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n729:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded read-only review candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n730:                 command: |\n731:                   node --experimental-strip-types --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n732:                   import {\n733:                     buildReviewPivotPreparationInput,\n734:                     renderReviewPivotSeatPrompt,\n735:                   } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts';\n736:                   import {\n737:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n738:                   } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n739: \n740:                   const input = buildReviewPivotPreparationInput({\n741:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n742:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n743:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n744:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n745:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.findings_registry}',\n746:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n747:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n748:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n749:                   });\n750:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n751:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n752:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n753:                         seat.id,\n754:                         renderReviewPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n755:                       ]))\n756:                     : {};\n757:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n758:                     ...prepared,\n759:                     seatPrompts,\n760:                     boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n761:                   })}\\n`);\n762:                   EOF\n763:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n764:                 outputs:\n765:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n766:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n767:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n768:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n769:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n770:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n771:                   - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n772:                   - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n773:                   - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n774:                   - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"\n\n(Showing lines 600-774 of 2111. Use offset=775 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"          4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n               signals = []\n               a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n                  avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n                  stop if avg <= 0.08\n               b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n                  noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n                  stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n               c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n                  coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n                  stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n               Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n               if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n               if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n               else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n          5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n               a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n               b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n               c) p0ResolutionGate: pass when activeP0 == 0; record activeP0\n               d) evidenceDensityGate: pass when every active P0/P1 has concrete file:line evidence and no active P0/P1 relies only on inference; record avgEvidencePerFinding","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","text":"          4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n               signals = []\n               a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n                  avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n                  stop if avg <= 0.08\n               b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n                  noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n                  stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n               c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n                  coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n                  stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n               Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n               if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n               if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n               else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n          5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n               a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n               b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n               c) p0ResolutionGate: pass when activeP0 == 0; record activeP0\n               d) evidenceDensityGate: pass when every active P0/P1 has concrete file:line evidence and no active P0/P1 relies only on inference; record avgEvidencePerFinding\n               e) hotspotSaturationGate: pass when review hotspots have been revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic\n               f) claimAdjudicationGate: pass when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == true (i.e. last_claim_adjudication_passed != false OR there are no active P0/P1 findings to adjudicate); record last_claim_adjudication_passed and claim_adjudication_active_count\n               g) fixCompletenessReplayGate: pass when security_sensitive_fix_scope == false OR every required closed-gate replay row passes with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage; record security_sensitive_fix_scope, fix_completeness_replay_required_rows, and fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows\n               h) candidateCoverageGate: skip entirely when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 on the latest iteration. Otherwise pass when the current iteration's `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass` is `trivial` with `enforcement: \"skip\"` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` is non-empty, OR when the reducer registry's `searchDebt` is empty AND `candidateCoverage.covered` is a superset of `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` for the lineage. Otherwise pass = false; record `searchDebt` items as blocked-stop evidence; blocker name = \"candidateCoverageGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Resolve deferred/blocked obligations in next iteration or downgrade scope explicitly to trivial with cited evidence.\"\n               i) graphlessFallbackGate: skip when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 OR the reducer registry's last-iteration `searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode` is `graph`. Applies when graphCoverageMode is `graphless_fallback` or `unavailable_blocked`. Pass when graphCoverageMode is `graphless_fallback` AND at least one `searchLedger` row exists for each entry in `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` with `searchActions[].method` in {\"direct_read\",\"exact_grep\",\"semantic_search\",\"code_graph_status_check\",\"producer_consumer_trace\",\"negative_test_inspection\"} AND non-empty `evidenceRefs`. Fail automatically when graphCoverageMode is `unavailable_blocked`; record the explicit unavailability reason. Otherwise pass = false; blocker name = \"graphlessFallbackGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Add cited fallback ledger rows (direct read, exact search, producer/consumer trace, negative-test inspection) or set graphCoverageMode to 'graph' once graph data is available.\"\n             if STOP is a candidate and any gate fails:\n               decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n               stop_blocked = true\n               stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n               blocked_by_json = JSON array of failing gate names (always include \"claimAdjudicationGate\" when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false, \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\" when fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass == false, \"candidateCoverageGate\" when candidate_coverage_gate_pass == false, and \"graphlessFallbackGate\" when graphless_fallback_gate_pass == false)\n               blocked_by_csv = comma-separated list of failing gate names\n               convergence_gate_pass = boolean\n               convergence_gate_score = numeric convergence score\n               dimension_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n               dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = JSON array of covered review dimensions\n               dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = JSON array of missing review dimensions\n               p0_resolution_gate_pass = boolean\n               active_p0_count = number of active P0 findings\n               evidence_density_gate_pass = boolean\n               avg_evidence_per_finding = numeric evidence density\n               hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = boolean\n               claim_adjudication_gate_pass = boolean\n               claim_adjudication_active_count = numeric count of active P0/P1 at the gate\n               fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = boolean\n               security_sensitive_fix_scope = boolean\n               fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = numeric count of closed-gate replay rows required for security-sensitive fix reruns\n               fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = numeric count of required closed-gate replay rows marked PASS with evidence\n               candidate_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n               candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations blocking STOP, else []\n               candidate_coverage_missing_json = JSON array of required bug classes not present in candidateCoverage.covered, else []\n               graphless_fallback_gate_pass = boolean\n               graphless_fallback_mode = latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\n               graphless_fallback_missing_json = JSON array of required bug classes without cited fallback ledger rows, else []\n               graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = explicit reason when graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n               recovery_strategy = one-line hint describing the next review action needed to satisfy the failed gates; combine candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate recovery guidance when both fail (when claimAdjudicationGate is the failing gate, prefer the step-0 recovery_strategy already set)\n          6. COMBINED STOP RULE:\n               a) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\": decision = \"STOP\"\n               b) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n                    decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n                    stop_blocked = true\n                    stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n                    # Blocked-stop closure: blockedBy must be string[] per the\n                    # published review blocked-stop contract. Extract the `.type`\n                    # field from each structured graph blocker; preserve the full\n                    # objects in graph_blocker_detail_json for operator inspection.\n                    blocked_by_json = JSON.stringify(graph_blockers_json.map(b => typeof b === \"string\" ? b : (b && b.type) || \"graph_blocker\"))\n                    blocked_by_csv = graph_blockers_csv\n                    graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n                    recovery_strategy = \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\"\n               c) if STOP is legal AND graph_decision == \"CONTINUE\":\n                    decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n                    stop_blocked = false\n                    reason = \"graph_convergence_continue\"\n               d) else keep the existing STUCK_RECOVERY or CONTINUE outcome\n        outputs:\n          - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n          - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n          - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n          - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n          - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n          - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n          - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n          - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n          - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n          - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n          - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n          - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n          - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n          - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n          - claim_adjudication_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for claimAdjudicationGate (false vetoes STOP)\"\n          - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings evaluated by claimAdjudicationGate\"\n          - fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for fixCompletenessReplayGate (false vetoes STOP on security-sensitive fix reruns)\"\n          - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the review is a security-sensitive fix rerun\"\n          - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count of closed-gate replay rows required before STOP\"\n          - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count of required closed-gate replay rows that passed with evidence\"\n          - candidate_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for candidateCoverageGate (false vetoes STOP for unresolved reducer-owned search debt or uncovered required bug classes)\"\n          - candidate_coverage_search_debt_json: \"JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations used as blocked-stop evidence\"\n          - candidate_coverage_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing from candidateCoverage.covered\"\n          - graphless_fallback_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for graphlessFallbackGate (false vetoes STOP when graphless fallback evidence is absent or unavailable_blocked)\"\n          - graphless_fallback_mode: \"Latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\"\n          - graphless_fallback_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing cited fallback ledger rows\"\n          - graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason: \"Explicit unavailability reason when graphCoverageMode == unavailable_blocked\"\n          - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED from step_graph_convergence\"\n          - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by graph convergence\"\n          - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers\"\n          - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker summary\"\n          - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next review action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n\n      step_emit_blocked_stop:\n        action: \"Persist blocked-stop evidence whenever the review legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP\"\n        if_blocked:\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergenceGate\":{\"pass\":{convergence_gate_pass},\"score\":{convergence_gate_score}},\"dimensionCoverageGate\":{\"pass\":{dimension_coverage_gate_pass},\"covered\":{dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json},\"missing\":{dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json}},\"p0ResolutionGate\":{\"pass\":{p0_resolution_gate_pass},\"activeP0\":{active_p0_count}},\"evidenceDensityGate\":{\"pass\":{evidence_density_gate_pass},\"avgEvidencePerFinding\":{avg_evidence_per_finding}},\"hotspotSaturationGate\":{\"pass\":{hotspot_saturation_gate_pass}},\"claimAdjudicationGate\":{\"pass\":{claim_adjudication_gate_pass},\"activeP0P1\":{claim_adjudication_active_count}},\"fixCompletenessReplayGate\":{\"pass\":{fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass},\"securitySensitive\":{security_sensitive_fix_scope},\"requiredRows\":{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows},\"passingRows\":{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}},\"candidateCoverageGate\":{\"pass\":{candidate_coverage_gate_pass},\"searchDebt\":{candidate_coverage_search_debt_json},\"missing\":{candidate_coverage_missing_json}},\"graphlessFallbackGate\":{\"pass\":{graphless_fallback_gate_pass},\"mode\":\"{graphless_fallback_mode}\",\"missing\":{graphless_fallback_missing_json},\"unavailabilityReason\":\"{graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason}\"}},\"graphBlockerDetail\":{graph_blockers_json},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n          log: \"Blocked STOP persisted for review loop. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n        if_not_blocked:\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_handle_convergence:\n        action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n        if_stop:\n          branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n          if_divergent_eligible:\n            eligibility_contract:\n              required_decision: \"STOP\"\n              eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n              excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n              fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n            steps:\n              step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n                action: \"Generate state-grounded read-only review candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n                command: |\n                  node --experimental-strip-types --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n                  import {\n                    buildReviewPivotPreparationInput,\n                    renderReviewPivotSeatPrompt,\n                  } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts';\n                  import {\n                    preparePivotTransaction,\n                  } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n\n                  const input = buildReviewPivotPreparationInput({\n                    artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n                    configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n                    stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n                    strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n                    registryPath: '{state_paths.findings_registry}',\n                    currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n                    maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n                    triggerReason: '{reason}',\n                  });\n                  const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n                  const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n                    ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n                        seat.id,\n                        renderReviewPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n                      ]))\n                    : {};\n                  process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n                    ...prepared,\n                    seatPrompts,\n                    boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n                  })}\\n`);\n                  EOF\n                working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n                outputs:\n                  - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n                  - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n                  - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n                  - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n                  - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n                  - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n                  - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n                  - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n                  - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n                  - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"","lineStart":600,"lineEnd":774,"totalLines":2111,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","time":{"start":1784387593879,"end":1784387593885}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a22406ee47343c4016a5b9809aee881919ce5b918de6dc84d"}},"id":"prt_f75c9e61a001tAf86chnmz17V8","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c9c057001vYQnpmVsQIkzpJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387593948,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_S8NKMGvL5DRsT8Ace7uBmCht","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","offset":1635,"limit":350},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1635:   phase_synthesis:\n1636:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1637:     steps:\n1638: \n1639:       step_fanout_merge:\n1640:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1641:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1642:         command: |\n1643:           node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1644:             --loop-type review \\\n1645:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1646:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1647:         wait_for_completion: true\n1648:         bind_from_output:\n1649:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1650:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1651:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1652: \n1653:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1654:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1655:         read:\n1656:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1657:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1658:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1659:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1660:         extract:\n1661:           - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n1662:           - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n1663:           - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n1664:           - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n1665:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1666:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1667:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and checklist.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1668:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1669:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n1670: \n1671:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1672:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1673:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n1674:       # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n1675:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1676:       step_derive_verdict:\n1677:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1678:         algorithm: |\n1679:           if p0_count > 0:\n1680:             verdict = \"FAIL\"\n1681:           elif p1_count > 0:\n1682:             verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n1683:           else:\n1684:             verdict = \"PASS\"\n1685:           has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n1686:           ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n1687:         outputs:\n1688:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n1689:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n1690:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n1691:         contract: |\n1692:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n1693:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n1694: \n1695:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1696:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1697:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1698:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1699: \n1700:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1701:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1702:         algorithm: |\n1703:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1704:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1705:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1706:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1707:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1708:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1709:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1710:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1711:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1712:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1713:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1714:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1715:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1716:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1717:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1718:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1719:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1720:              - Determine final severity and status\n1721:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n1722:         outputs:\n1723:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1724:           - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n1725:           - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n1726:           - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n1727: \n1728:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1729:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1730:         algorithm: |\n1731:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1732:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1733:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1734:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1735:           Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n1736: \n1737:       step_emit_resource_map:\n1738:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n1739:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --emit-resource-map\"\n1740:         read:\n1741:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1742:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n1743:         write:\n1744:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n1745:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n1746: \n1747:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n1748:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n1749:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n1750: \n1751:       step_compile_review_report:\n1752:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n1753:         instructions: |\n1754:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n1755: \n1756:           1. **Executive Summary**\n1757:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n1758:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n1759:              - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n1760:              - Review scope summary\n1761: \n1762:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n1763:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n1764:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n1765:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n1766:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n1767: \n1768:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n1769:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n1770:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n1771: \n1772:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n1773:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n1774: \n1775:           5. **Spec Seed**\n1776:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n1777: \n1778:           6. **Plan Seed**\n1779:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n1780: \n1781:            7. **Traceability Status**\n1782:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n1783:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n1784:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n1785: \n1786:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n1787:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n1788:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n1789:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n1790: \n1791:           8. **Deferred Items**\n1792:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n1793: \n1794:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n1795:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n1796:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n1797:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n1798: \n1799:           9. **Search Ledger**\n1800:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n1801:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n1802:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n1803:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n1804: \n1805:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n1806:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n1807:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n1808: \n1809:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop_protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n1810:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n1811: \n1812:       step_convergence_report:\n1813:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n1814:         command: |\n1815:           node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1816:           import { appendFileSync, existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\n1817: \n1818:           const paths = {\n1819:             stateLog: String.raw`{state_paths.state_log}`,\n1820:             registry: String.raw`{state_paths.findings_registry}`,\n1821:             review: String.raw`{state_paths.review_output}`,\n1822:             dashboard: String.raw`{state_paths.dashboard}`,\n1823:           };\n1824: \n1825:           function hasFile(filePath) {\n1826:             try {\n1827:               return existsSync(filePath) && statSync(filePath).isFile();\n1828:             } catch {\n1829:               return false;\n1830:             }\n1831:           }\n1832: \n1833:           function readJson(filePath) {\n1834:             try {\n1835:               return JSON.parse(readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\n1836:             } catch {\n1837:               return null;\n1838:             }\n1839:           }\n1840: \n1841:           function readJsonl(filePath) {\n1842:             if (!hasFile(filePath)) return [];\n1843:             return readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8')\n1844:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n1845:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n1846:               .filter(Boolean)\n1847:               .flatMap((line) => {\n1848:                 try {\n1849:                   return [JSON.parse(line)];\n1850:                 } catch {\n1851:                   return [];\n1852:                 }\n1853:               });\n1854:           }\n1855: \n1856:           function countIterationFindings(record) {\n1857:             if (!record || record.type !== 'iteration') return 0;\n1858:             const numeric = Number(record.findingsCount);\n1859:             if (Number.isFinite(numeric) && numeric > 0) return Math.floor(numeric);\n1860:             if (Array.isArray(record.findingDetails)) return record.findingDetails.length;\n1861:             return 0;\n1862:           }\n1863: \n1864:           function normalizeFindingKey(value) {\n1865:             return String(value || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ');\n1866:           }\n1867: \n1868:           function findingKeys(candidate) {\n1869:             if (typeof candidate === 'string') {\n1870:               const key = normalizeFindingKey(candidate);\n1871:               return key ? [key] : [];\n1872:             }\n1873:             if (!candidate || typeof candidate !== 'object' || Array.isArray(candidate)) return [];\n1874:             return [...new Set([\n1875:               candidate.id,\n1876:               candidate.findingId,\n1877:               candidate.title,\n1878:               candidate.summary,\n1879:               candidate.text,\n1880:               candidate.finding,\n1881:               candidate.description,\n1882:             ].map(normalizeFindingKey).filter(Boolean))];\n1883:           }\n1884: \n1885:           function collectIterationFindingGroups(record) {\n1886:             if (!record || record.type !== 'iteration' || !Array.isArray(record.findingDetails)) return [];\n1887:             return record.findingDetails\n1888:               .map(findingKeys)\n1889:               .filter((keys) => keys.length > 0);\n1890:           }\n1891: \n1892:           function collectRegistryFindingKeys(registry) {\n1893:             return [registry?.openFindings, registry?.resolvedFindings, registry?.repeatedFindings]\n1894:               .filter(Array.isArray)\n1895:               .flatMap((findings) => findings)\n1896:               .flatMap(findingKeys);\n1897:           }\n1898: \n1899:           function appendEvent(event) {\n1900:             appendFileSync(paths.stateLog, `${JSON.stringify(event)}\\n`, 'utf8');\n1901:           }\n1902: \n1903:           const registry = readJson(paths.registry);\n1904:           const openCount = Array.isArray(registry?.openFindings) ? registry.openFindings.length : null;\n1905:           const resolvedCount = Array.isArray(registry?.resolvedFindings) ? registry.resolvedFindings.length : 0;\n1906:           const repeatedCount = Array.isArray(registry?.repeatedFindings) ? registry.repeatedFindings.length : 0;\n1907:           const registryFindingCount = openCount === null ? null : openCount + resolvedCount + repeatedCount;\n1908:           const stateRecords = readJsonl(paths.stateLog);\n1909:           const iterationFindingCount = stateRecords.reduce((sum, record) => sum + countIterationFindings(record), 0);\n1910:           const identifiableFindingGroups = stateRecords.flatMap(collectIterationFindingGroups);\n1911:           const registryFindingKeys = new Set(collectRegistryFindingKeys(registry));\n1912:           const missingStructuredFindingCount = identifiableFindingGroups.filter((keys) => !keys.some((key) => registryFindingKeys.has(key))).length;\n1913:           const identifiableFindingCount = identifiableFindingGroups.length;\n1914:           const missingArtifacts = [\n1915:             ['registry', paths.registry],\n1916:             ['review', paths.review],\n1917:             ['dashboard', paths.dashboard],\n1918:           ].filter(([, filePath]) => !hasFile(filePath)).map(([name, filePath]) => ({ name, path: filePath }));\n1919:           const invariantFailures = [];\n1920:           if (missingArtifacts.length > 0) invariantFailures.push('missing_synthesis_artifacts');\n1921:           if (registryFindingCount === null) invariantFailures.push('registry_missing_openFindings');\n1922:           if (iterationFindingCount > 0 && (registryFindingCount ?? 0) === 0) invariantFailures.push('state_findings_not_reflected_in_registry');\n1923:           if (identifiableFindingCount > 0 && registryFindingCount !== null && registryFindingCount < identifiableFindingCount) invariantFailures.push('structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry');\n1924:           if (missingStructuredFindingCount > 0) invariantFailures.push('structured_state_findings_missing_from_registry');\n1925: \n1926:           if (invariantFailures.length > 0) {\n1927:             appendEvent({\n1928:               type: 'event',\n1929:               event: 'synthesis_incomplete',\n1930:               mode: 'review',\n1931:               severity: 'warning',\n1932:               totalIterations: Number('{iteration_count}'),\n1933:               activeP0: Number('{active_p0}'),\n1934:               activeP1: Number('{active_p1}'),\n1935:               activeP2: Number('{active_p2}'),\n1936:               dimensionCoverage: Number('{dimension_coverage}'),\n1937:               verdict: '{verdict}',\n1938:               releaseReadinessState: '{release_readiness_state}',\n1939:               stopReason: '{reason}',\n1940:               reason: 'synthesis_artifact_invariant_failed',\n1941:               invariantFailures,\n1942:               missingArtifacts,\n1943:               registryFindingCount,\n1944:               iterationFindingCount,\n1945:               identifiableFindingCount,\n1946:               missingStructuredFindingCount,\n1947:               timestamp: '{ISO_8601_NOW}',\n1948:             });\n1949:           } else {\n1950:             appendEvent({\n1951:               type: 'event',\n1952:               event: 'synthesis_complete',\n1953:               mode: 'review',\n1954:               totalIterations: Number('{iteration_count}'),\n1955:               activeP0: Number('{active_p0}'),\n1956:               activeP1: Number('{active_p1}'),\n1957:               activeP2: Number('{active_p2}'),\n1958:               dimensionCoverage: Number('{dimension_coverage}'),\n1959:               verdict: '{verdict}',\n1960:               releaseReadinessState: '{release_readiness_state}',\n1961:               stopReason: '{reason}',\n1962:               timestamp: '{ISO_8601_NOW}',\n1963:             });\n1964:           }\n1965:           EOF\n1966:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n1967: \n1968:       step_update_config_status:\n1969:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n1970:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1971:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n1972: \n1973:       step_leave_artifacts_unstaged:\n1974:         action: \"Leave all synthesized artifacts unstaged for explicit operator review\"\n1975:         note: \"Synthesis must not mutate the shared Git index. The operator retains staging and commit authority after reviewing the complete artifact directory.\"\n1976: \n1977:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n1978:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n1979:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n1980:   phase_save:\n1981:     purpose: Preserve review context to memory system\n1982:     steps:\n1983: \n1984:       step_compose_save_payload:\n\n(Showing lines 1635-1984 of 2111. Use offset=1985 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","text":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n          - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and checklist.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n          - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n\n      # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n      # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n      # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n      # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n      # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n      step_derive_verdict:\n        action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if p0_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"FAIL\"\n          elif p1_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n          else:\n            verdict = \"PASS\"\n          has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n          ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n        outputs:\n          - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n          - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n        contract: |\n          Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n          Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n\n      step_read_all_iterations:\n        action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n        read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n        read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_build_finding_registry:\n        action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n          2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n             content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n             Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n          3. Two-tier dedup:\n             PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n               - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n             FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n               - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n          4. Track finding lifecycle:\n             - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n             - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n             - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n          5. Resolve contradictions:\n             - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n             - Determine final severity and status\n          6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n        outputs:\n          - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n          - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n          - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n          - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n\n      step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n        action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          For each active P0/P1 finding:\n            1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n            2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n            3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n          Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n\n      step_emit_resource_map:\n        action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n        command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --emit-resource-map\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n        guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n\n      step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n        action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n        note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop_protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_convergence_report:\n        action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n        command: |\n          node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n          import { appendFileSync, existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\n\n          const paths = {\n            stateLog: String.raw`{state_paths.state_log}`,\n            registry: String.raw`{state_paths.findings_registry}`,\n            review: String.raw`{state_paths.review_output}`,\n            dashboard: String.raw`{state_paths.dashboard}`,\n          };\n\n          function hasFile(filePath) {\n            try {\n              return existsSync(filePath) && statSync(filePath).isFile();\n            } catch {\n              return false;\n            }\n          }\n\n          function readJson(filePath) {\n            try {\n              return JSON.parse(readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\n            } catch {\n              return null;\n            }\n          }\n\n          function readJsonl(filePath) {\n            if (!hasFile(filePath)) return [];\n            return readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8')\n              .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n              .map((line) => line.trim())\n              .filter(Boolean)\n              .flatMap((line) => {\n                try {\n                  return [JSON.parse(line)];\n                } catch {\n                  return [];\n                }\n              });\n          }\n\n          function countIterationFindings(record) {\n            if (!record || record.type !== 'iteration') return 0;\n            const numeric = Number(record.findingsCount);\n            if (Number.isFinite(numeric) && numeric > 0) return Math.floor(numeric);\n            if (Array.isArray(record.findingDetails)) return record.findingDetails.length;\n            return 0;\n          }\n\n          function normalizeFindingKey(value) {\n            return String(value || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ');\n          }\n\n          function findingKeys(candidate) {\n            if (typeof candidate === 'string') {\n              const key = normalizeFindingKey(candidate);\n              return key ? [key] : [];\n            }\n            if (!candidate || typeof candidate !== 'object' || Array.isArray(candidate)) return [];\n            return [...new Set([\n              candidate.id,\n              candidate.findingId,\n              candidate.title,\n              candidate.summary,\n              candidate.text,\n              candidate.finding,\n              candidate.description,\n            ].map(normalizeFindingKey).filter(Boolean))];\n          }\n\n          function collectIterationFindingGroups(record) {\n            if (!record || record.type !== 'iteration' || !Array.isArray(record.findingDetails)) return [];\n            return record.findingDetails\n              .map(findingKeys)\n              .filter((keys) => keys.length > 0);\n          }\n\n          function collectRegistryFindingKeys(registry) {\n            return [registry?.openFindings, registry?.resolvedFindings, registry?.repeatedFindings]\n              .filter(Array.isArray)\n              .flatMap((findings) => findings)\n              .flatMap(findingKeys);\n          }\n\n          function appendEvent(event) {\n            appendFileSync(paths.stateLog, `${JSON.stringify(event)}\\n`, 'utf8');\n          }\n\n          const registry = readJson(paths.registry);\n          const openCount = Array.isArray(registry?.openFindings) ? registry.openFindings.length : null;\n          const resolvedCount = Array.isArray(registry?.resolvedFindings) ? registry.resolvedFindings.length : 0;\n          const repeatedCount = Array.isArray(registry?.repeatedFindings) ? registry.repeatedFindings.length : 0;\n          const registryFindingCount = openCount === null ? null : openCount + resolvedCount + repeatedCount;\n          const stateRecords = readJsonl(paths.stateLog);\n          const iterationFindingCount = stateRecords.reduce((sum, record) => sum + countIterationFindings(record), 0);\n          const identifiableFindingGroups = stateRecords.flatMap(collectIterationFindingGroups);\n          const registryFindingKeys = new Set(collectRegistryFindingKeys(registry));\n          const missingStructuredFindingCount = identifiableFindingGroups.filter((keys) => !keys.some((key) => registryFindingKeys.has(key))).length;\n          const identifiableFindingCount = identifiableFindingGroups.length;\n          const missingArtifacts = [\n            ['registry', paths.registry],\n            ['review', paths.review],\n            ['dashboard', paths.dashboard],\n          ].filter(([, filePath]) => !hasFile(filePath)).map(([name, filePath]) => ({ name, path: filePath }));\n          const invariantFailures = [];\n          if (missingArtifacts.length > 0) invariantFailures.push('missing_synthesis_artifacts');\n          if (registryFindingCount === null) invariantFailures.push('registry_missing_openFindings');\n          if (iterationFindingCount > 0 && (registryFindingCount ?? 0) === 0) invariantFailures.push('state_findings_not_reflected_in_registry');\n          if (identifiableFindingCount > 0 && registryFindingCount !== null && registryFindingCount < identifiableFindingCount) invariantFailures.push('structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry');\n          if (missingStructuredFindingCount > 0) invariantFailures.push('structured_state_findings_missing_from_registry');\n\n          if (invariantFailures.length > 0) {\n            appendEvent({\n              type: 'event',\n              event: 'synthesis_incomplete',\n              mode: 'review',\n              severity: 'warning',\n              totalIterations: Number('{iteration_count}'),\n              activeP0: Number('{active_p0}'),\n              activeP1: Number('{active_p1}'),\n              activeP2: Number('{active_p2}'),\n              dimensionCoverage: Number('{dimension_coverage}'),\n              verdict: '{verdict}',\n              releaseReadinessState: '{release_readiness_state}',\n              stopReason: '{reason}',\n              reason: 'synthesis_artifact_invariant_failed',\n              invariantFailures,\n              missingArtifacts,\n              registryFindingCount,\n              iterationFindingCount,\n              identifiableFindingCount,\n              missingStructuredFindingCount,\n              timestamp: '{ISO_8601_NOW}',\n            });\n          } else {\n            appendEvent({\n              type: 'event',\n              event: 'synthesis_complete',\n              mode: 'review',\n              totalIterations: Number('{iteration_count}'),\n              activeP0: Number('{active_p0}'),\n              activeP1: Number('{active_p1}'),\n              activeP2: Number('{active_p2}'),\n              dimensionCoverage: Number('{dimension_coverage}'),\n              verdict: '{verdict}',\n              releaseReadinessState: '{release_readiness_state}',\n              stopReason: '{reason}',\n              timestamp: '{ISO_8601_NOW}',\n            });\n          }\n          EOF\n        note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n\n      step_update_config_status:\n        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n\n      step_leave_artifacts_unstaged:\n        action: \"Leave all synthesized artifacts unstaged for explicit operator review\"\n        note: \"Synthesis must not mutate the shared Git index. The operator retains staging and commit authority after reviewing the complete artifact directory.\"\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 4: SAVE\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_save:\n    purpose: Preserve review context to memory system\n    steps:\n\n      step_compose_save_payload:","lineStart":1635,"lineEnd":1984,"totalLines":2111,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_review_auto.yaml","time":{"start":1784387593941,"end":1784387593947}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a22406ee47343c4016a5b9809af0081919862d97adffa5c03"}},"id":"prt_f75c9e6a2001I306C0XUOSIcVF","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c9c057001vYQnpmVsQIkzpJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387594032,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UEYWOks2dCwihuBxxEvDyiAY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state_outputs.md","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state_outputs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\n3: description: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state outputs\"\n6:   - \"review packet outputs\"\n7:   - \"review dashboard output\"\n8:   - \"review report output\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.3\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review State Outputs\n15: \n16: This reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state_format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: Deep-review outputs are audit artifacts. Iteration agents write evidence, the reducer writes derived state, and synthesis writes the release-readiness report.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. PACKET FILES\n27: \n28: | File | Owner | Mutability | Purpose |\n29: |------|-------|------------|---------|\n30: | `deep-review-config.json` | Workflow | Immutable after init | Run parameters, lineage, threshold settings |\n31: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | Workflow and iteration contract | Append-only | Config, iteration, blocked-stop, pause, synthesis events |\n32: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | Reducer | Regenerated | Active, resolved, repeated, and blocked findings |\n33: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Reducer with operator-readable sections | Regenerated/updated | Dimension order, known context, next focus |\n34: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Reducer | Regenerated | Current status, trend, verdict preview |\n35: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Iteration agent | Write-once | Detailed findings for one pass |\n36: | `review-report.md` | Synthesis | Final output | Findings-first release-readiness report |\n37: | `resource-map.md` | Synthesis | Final or disabled | Converged delta evidence map |\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 3. ITERATION MARKDOWN\n42: \n43: Each iteration file must be non-empty and end with exactly one final verdict line:\n44: \n45: ```text\n46: Review verdict: PASS\n47: ```\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ```text\n54: Review verdict: FAIL\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The line maps to the findings in that iteration only. Synthesis computes the final release verdict from the full state.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 4. DASHBOARD\n62: \n63: The dashboard is a status view, not the source of truth. It should display:\n64: \n65: - Current iteration and next focus.\n66: - Active P0/P1/P2 counts.\n67: - Dimension coverage.\n68: - Convergence trend.\n69: - Gate blockers.\n70: - Provisional verdict.\n71: \n72: If dashboard data disagrees with JSONL, JSONL wins and the reducer must regenerate the dashboard.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 5. FINAL REPORT\n77: \n78: `review-report.md` is the handoff artifact. It carries:\n79: \n80: - Executive summary.\n81: - Planning trigger.\n82: - Active finding registry.\n83: - Remediation workstreams.\n84: - Spec seed.\n85: - Plan seed.\n86: - Traceability status.\n87: - Deferred items.\n88: - Audit appendix.\n89: - Optional Resource Map Coverage Gate section when a map existed at init.\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n94: \n95: - `references/state/state_format.md` for schemas.\n96: - `references/state/state_reducer_registry.md` for reducer ownership.\n97: - `references/convergence/convergence_signals.md` for STOP fields shown in dashboard/report.\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state outputs\"\n  - \"review packet outputs\"\n  - \"review dashboard output\"\n  - \"review report output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Outputs\n\nThis reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state_format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state_outputs.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state outputs\"\n  - \"review packet outputs\"\n  - \"review dashboard output\"\n  - \"review report output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Outputs\n\nThis reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state_format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDeep-review outputs are audit artifacts. Iteration agents write evidence, the reducer writes derived state, and synthesis writes the release-readiness report.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKET FILES\n\n| File | Owner | Mutability | Purpose |\n|------|-------|------------|---------|\n| `deep-review-config.json` | Workflow | Immutable after init | Run parameters, lineage, threshold settings |\n| `deep-review-state.jsonl` | Workflow and iteration contract | Append-only | Config, iteration, blocked-stop, pause, synthesis events |\n| `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | Reducer | Regenerated | Active, resolved, repeated, and blocked findings |\n| `deep-review-strategy.md` | Reducer with operator-readable sections | Regenerated/updated | Dimension order, known context, next focus |\n| `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Reducer | Regenerated | Current status, trend, verdict preview |\n| `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Iteration agent | Write-once | Detailed findings for one pass |\n| `review-report.md` | Synthesis | Final output | Findings-first release-readiness report |\n| `resource-map.md` | Synthesis | Final or disabled | Converged delta evidence map |\n\n---\n\n## 3. ITERATION MARKDOWN\n\nEach iteration file must be non-empty and end with exactly one final verdict line:\n\n```text\nReview verdict: PASS\n```\n\n```text\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n```\n\n```text\nReview verdict: FAIL\n```\n\nThe line maps to the findings in that iteration only. Synthesis computes the final release verdict from the full state.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DASHBOARD\n\nThe dashboard is a status view, not the source of truth. It should display:\n\n- Current iteration and next focus.\n- Active P0/P1/P2 counts.\n- Dimension coverage.\n- Convergence trend.\n- Gate blockers.\n- Provisional verdict.\n\nIf dashboard data disagrees with JSONL, JSONL wins and the reducer must regenerate the dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## 5. FINAL REPORT\n\n`review-report.md` is the handoff artifact. It carries:\n\n- Executive summary.\n- Planning trigger.\n- Active finding registry.\n- Remediation workstreams.\n- Spec seed.\n- Plan seed.\n- Traceability status.\n- Deferred items.\n- Audit appendix.\n- Optional Resource Map Coverage Gate section when a map existed at init.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/state/state_format.md` for schemas.\n- `references/state/state_reducer_registry.md` for reducer ownership.\n- `references/convergence/convergence_signals.md` for STOP fields shown in dashboard/report.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":97,"totalLines":97,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state_outputs.md","time":{"start":1784387594026,"end":1784387594031}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a22406ee47343c4016a5b9809af0c81919970f8aa0a3ba9a1"}},"id":"prt_f75c9e6ee0013lWUNO7MG2Basn","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c9c057001vYQnpmVsQIkzpJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784387594147,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_qSc44e5jnICTzC5xD1c3DcU2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","offset":600,"limit":50},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n600: \n601: // A lineage's synthesis stopReason is written by its model and cannot be held to an exact\n602: // spelling. The iteration-count check above already proves the lineage ran every iteration,\n603: // so this only needs to confirm the reason belongs to the max-iterations family (e.g.\n604: // \"maxIterationsReached\", \"max-iterations (10/10)\") and is not a genuinely different outcome\n605: // such as convergence, a manual stop, or an error.\n606: function isMaxIterationsStopReason(stopReason) {\n607:   if (typeof stopReason !== 'string') return false;\n608:   return stopReason.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '').startsWith('maxiteration');\n609: }\n610: \n611: function findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({ loopType, stateRead, lineage, stopPolicy }) {\n612:   if (loopType !== 'review' || stopPolicy !== 'max-iterations') return null;\n613:   if (typeof lineage.iterations !== 'number' || lineage.iterations <= 0) {\n614:     return 'stopPolicy=max-iterations requires a positive lineage iteration cap';\n615:   }\n616: \n617:   if (!stateRead || stateRead.missing) {\n618:     return 'missing deep-review-state.jsonl for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n619:   }\n620:   if (stateRead.parseError) {\n621:     return `could not parse deep-review-state.jsonl: ${stateRead.parseError}`;\n622:   }\n623: \n624:   const records = stateRead.records;\n625:   const iterationCount = records.filter((record) => record && record.type === 'iteration').length;\n626:   const synthesis = [...records]\n627:     .reverse()\n628:     .find((record) => record && record.type === 'event' && record.event === 'synthesis_complete');\n629:   if (!synthesis) {\n630:     return 'missing synthesis_complete event for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n631:   }\n632: \n633:   const totalIterations = Number.isFinite(Number(synthesis.totalIterations))\n634:     ? Number(synthesis.totalIterations)\n635:     : iterationCount;\n636:   if (totalIterations !== lineage.iterations) {\n637:     return `expected ${lineage.iterations} iterations, got ${totalIterations}`;\n638:   }\n639:   if (!isMaxIterationsStopReason(synthesis.stopReason)) {\n640:     return `expected stopReason=maxIterationsReached, got ${synthesis.stopReason || 'unknown'}`;\n641:   }\n642:   return null;\n643: }\n644: \n645: function isRecord(value) {\n646:   return value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n647: }\n648: \n649: function normalizeStallWatchdogMs(rawConfig) {\n\n(Showing lines 600-649 of 2021. Use offset=650 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n// A lineage's synthesis stopReason is written by its model and cannot be held to an exact\n// spelling. The iteration-count check above already proves the lineage ran every iteration,\n// so this only needs to confirm the reason belongs to the max-iterations family (e.g.\n// \"maxIterationsReached\", \"max-iterations (10/10)\") and is not a genuinely different outcome\n// such as convergence, a manual stop, or an error.\nfunction isMaxIterationsStopReason(stopReason) {\n  if (typeof stopReason !== 'string') return false;\n  return stopReason.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '').startsWith('maxiteration');\n}\n\nfunction findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({ loopType, stateRead, lineage, stopPolicy }) {\n  if (loopType !== 'review' || stopPolicy !== 'max-iterations') return null;\n  if (typeof lineage.iterations !== 'number' || lineage.iterations <= 0) {\n    return 'stopPolicy=max-iterations requires a positive lineage iteration cap';\n  }\n\n  if (!stateRead || stateRead.missing) {\n    return 'missing deep-review-state.jsonl for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n  }","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","text":"\n// A lineage's synthesis stopReason is written by its model and cannot be held to an exact\n// spelling. The iteration-count check above already proves the lineage ran every iteration,\n// so this only needs to confirm the reason belongs to the max-iterations family (e.g.\n// \"maxIterationsReached\", \"max-iterations (10/10)\") and is not a genuinely different outcome\n// such as convergence, a manual stop, or an error.\nfunction isMaxIterationsStopReason(stopReason) {\n  if (typeof stopReason !== 'string') return false;\n  return stopReason.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '').startsWith('maxiteration');\n}\n\nfunction findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({ loopType, stateRead, lineage, stopPolicy }) {\n  if (loopType !== 'review' || stopPolicy !== 'max-iterations') return null;\n  if (typeof lineage.iterations !== 'number' || lineage.iterations <= 0) {\n    return 'stopPolicy=max-iterations requires a positive lineage iteration cap';\n  }\n\n  if (!stateRead || stateRead.missing) {\n    return 'missing deep-review-state.jsonl for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n  }\n  if (stateRead.parseError) {\n    return `could not parse deep-review-state.jsonl: ${stateRead.parseError}`;\n  }\n\n  const records = stateRead.records;\n  const iterationCount = records.filter((record) => record && record.type === 'iteration').length;\n  const synthesis = [...records]\n    .reverse()\n    .find((record) => record && record.type === 'event' && record.event === 'synthesis_complete');\n  if (!synthesis) {\n    return 'missing synthesis_complete event for max-iterations stop-policy validation';\n  }\n\n  const totalIterations = Number.isFinite(Number(synthesis.totalIterations))\n    ? Number(synthesis.totalIterations)\n    : iterationCount;\n  if (totalIterations !== lineage.iterations) {\n    return `expected ${lineage.iterations} iterations, got ${totalIterations}`;\n  }\n  if (!isMaxIterationsStopReason(synthesis.stopReason)) {\n    return `expected stopReason=maxIterationsReached, got ${synthesis.stopReason || 'unknown'}`;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value) {\n  return value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeStallWatchdogMs(rawConfig) {","lineStart":600,"lineEnd":649,"totalLines":2021,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","time":{"start":1784387594131,"end":1784387594145}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a22406ee47343c4016a5b9809af10819195446fd43824c0f0"}},"id":"prt_f75c9e749001f45aWfBmw2DdoD","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","messageID":"msg_f75c9c057001vYQnpmVsQIkzpJ"}}
