{"type":"text","timestamp":1784387615756,"sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","part":{"id":"prt_f75ca35b1001WU0H0Qnv92dVUd","messageID":"msg_f75c9f0bf001GMuEExkQ2slYR4","sessionID":"ses_08a55b97effep2EaPBEqRiOfI4","type":"text","text":"The legal-stop audit found one schema-level blocker: iteration 5’s fallback ledger used descriptive method names (`exact_search`, `live_row_count`, `negative_search`) instead of the contract’s allowed enums (`exact_grep`, `direct_read`, `negative_test_inspection`). The evidence itself is sufficient, but STOP must fail closed; I’m persisting the blocked-stop event and running one corrective stabilization iteration with canonical method names.","time":{"start":1784387614129,"end":1784387615755},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_09d2196abbe448cc016a5b981e177c8191a272e9ed8f3f2ecd","phase":"commentary"}}}}
